eventmse.lbx      0  00004      68  en            You are tuned to GNN, your source for all the news you need to know.
eventmse.lbx      1  00004      68  en            Galactic News Network, the galaxy's most watched information source.
eventmse.lbx      2  00004      32  en            GNN. Where the news comes first.
eventmse.lbx      3  00004      67  en            This is GNN, bringing you today's headlines from across the galaxy.
eventmse.lbx      4  00004      28  en            And elsewhere in the galaxy,
eventmse.lbx      5  00004      28  ?             Also making headlines today,
eventmse.lbx      6  00004      34  en            And now, in a GNN exclusive story,
eventmse.lbx      7  00004      69  en            GNN was also first on the scene to bring you this important headline:
eventmse.lbx      8  00037     104  en             Empire, when archeologists uncovered the secret of \x8D in the wreckage of an ancient, mysterious ship.
eventmse.lbx      9  00014      89  en             Empire have salvaged the key to \x8D and \x8E from the remains of an ancient alien ship.
eventmse.lbx     12  00011     135  en             Empire rejoiced when a sudden shift of the \x80 colony's planetary axis resulted in an improvement of its environment to terran norms.
eventmse.lbx     19  00011      62  en             citizens died today when a huge comet struck the \x80 colony.
eventmse.lbx     20  00014     152  en             Empire were shocked to discover a virus in the \x86 research center's computers. All systems were infected, totaling a loss of \x81 research point\x83.
eventmse.lbx     40  00004      88  en            A military \x85 ship mysteriously exploded. An investigation into the cause is underway.
eventmse.lbx     41  00004      79  en            A ship in the \x85 fleet inexplicably exploded, killing legendary officer \x89.
eventmse.lbx     46  00004     134  en            The galaxy has sighed in collective relief as the hyperspace flux that sealed entry into hyperspace ended as mysteriously as it began.
eventmse.lbx     47  00004     138  en            Devastating news for the entire galaxy today, as a hyperspace flux has shut off passage into hyperspace, preventing all ships from moving.
eventmse.lbx     52  0001B      71  en             miners, the mineral classification of \x8B colony was lowered to \x8C.
eventmse.lbx     56  00011     132  en             Empire discovered a previously unknown deposit of minerals on \x8B that improved the mineral classification of that planet to \x8C.
eventmse.lbx     64  00004     150  en            Pirates operating in the \x8B star system have begun to target freighters. Citizens call for more ships to be placed in the area to stop the thievery.
eventmse.lbx     65  00004     124  en            Pirate activity in the \x8B system has reduced annual trade revenues. Merchants are demanding more ships to patrol the area.
eventmse.lbx     66  00004     122  en            The people of the \x8B star system are celebrating the elimination of the pirates that had been plaguing their freighters.
eventmse.lbx     74  00014     103  en             Empire have found the cure for the plague on \x80. The pestilence will end, and not a moment too soon.
eventmse.lbx     76  0002C      91  en             Empire, as a sudden population boom has doubled the population growth rate of \x80 colony.
eventmse.lbx     84  00004     149  en            A state of emergency was declared when long range scanners began tracking a huge, toxic amoebic life form traveling at warp speed towards the galaxy.
eventmse.lbx     86  00004     140  en            For some inexplicable reason the Space Amoeba has left our galaxy. Let us pray that next time, we are better prepared for such an emergency.
eventmse.lbx     87  00004     130  en            The Space Amoeba engulfed the system of \x8B. Although the Amoeba was destroyed, the system will forever have a toxic environment.
eventmse.lbx     88  00004     137  en            Galactic scanners have picked up a crystal life form traveling at warp speed into our galaxy. It is not known where it will attack first.
eventmse.lbx     89  0000F      84  en             star fleet have destroyed the Space Crystal that was threatening the entire galaxy.
eventmse.lbx     90  00004     108  en            The hideous Space Crystal has left our galaxy. Why did it come? Why did it leave? The galaxy may never know.
eventmse.lbx     91  00004     135  en            The Space Crystal has killed millions of colonists in \x8B. The colony's structures remained intact, as lifeless monuments to the dead.
eventmse.lbx     92  00004      97  en            A giant Space Dragon has invaded the galaxy. Experts speculate that it is searching for treasure.
eventmse.lbx     93  00011      64  en             command have suceeded in destroying the monstrous Space Dragon.
eventmse.lbx     94  00004      73  en            The Space Dragon that threatened the galaxy has mysteriously disappeared.
eventmse.lbx     95  00012      67  en             Empire mourn for family killed by the Space Dragon attack on \x8B.
eventmse.lbx     96  00004     177  en            Long range scanners are monitoring the approach of a space monster that scientists have described as a giant eel-like creature. It appears to be searching for a spawning ground.
eventmse.lbx     98  00004     120  en            Scanners that have been tracking the progress of a Space Eel now show that the creature has disappeared from our galaxy.
eventmse.lbx     99  00004     106  en            The \x8B system has been blockaded by a dreadful Space Eel. The system's entire population cowers in fear.
eventmse.lbx    100  00004     171  en            A giant Space Hydra is being tracked entering the galaxy. It is unknown at this time which system it will target, but the results will be devastating if it is not stopped.
eventmse.lbx    102  00004      75  en            The Space Hydra has drifted out of our galaxy, departing for parts unknown.
eventmse.lbx    104  00004     174  en            Scientists predict that the star in the \x8B system will go super nova within \x81 year\x83. If a research solution cannot be found, colonies in the system will be destroyed.
eventmse.lbx    105  00004     137  en            Scientists have only \x81 year\x83 to prevent the \x8B star from going  super nova. \x82 more research point\x84 should bring a solution.
eventmse.lbx    106  00004     122  en            Scientists in the \x8B system have developed a solar rejuvenator that has ended the threat of their star going super nova.
eventmse.lbx    107  00004      86  en            The \x8B star has gone super nova, destroying most of the system and killing millions.
eventmse.lbx    110  00004     157  en            The time-space anomaly that held the \x8B star system frozen in time has ended. Contact has been reestablished, and colony production has returned to normal.
eventmse.lbx    111  00004     181  en            A time space anomaly has occurred in the \x8B star system. All colonies in that system are unable to build, and ships are unable to make contact for either trade or combat purposes.
eventmse.lbx    114  00004     112  en            The threat of the Hyperspace beast has ended. All space fleets may travel in hyperspace without fear once again.
eventmse.lbx    115  00004     154  en            A beast that exists partially in hyperspace has appeared. It is feared that it will randomly destroy ships in hyperspace for an indefinite period of time.
eventmse.lbx    124  00006      38  en             Empire has been completely destroyed.
eventmse.lbx    125  00006      65  en             Empire has fallen, and will no longer wield power in the galaxy.
eventmse.lbx    126  00006      69  ?              flag waves no more. No colonies or fleets remain in the \x85 Empire.
eventmse.lbx    127  00006     103  en             Empire will live on only in the history books, as the last vestige of \x85 power has been annihilated.
eventmse.lbx    128  00006      98  en             Empire has grown in strength. It now controls \x81 star systems, and shows no signs of weakening.
eventmse.lbx    129  00006      72  en             Empire now spans \x81 star systems, outnumbering all the other Empires.
eventmse.lbx    130  00006      66  ?              Empire now numbers \x81 star systems, more than any other Empire.
eventmse.lbx    131  00006      42  en             Empire controls a majority of the galaxy.
eventmse.lbx    132  00004      38  en            Current rankings of empire production:
eventmse.lbx    133  00004      42  en            The census rankings of empire populations:
eventmse.lbx    134  00004      39  en            Current leaders of advanced technology:
eventmse.lbx    135  00004      41  en            Current ranking of space fleet strengths:
eventmse.lbx    136  0000F      62  en             Empire have recently visited the legendary Orion star system.
eventmse.lbx    137  0000F      62  en             Empire have recently visited the legendary Orion star system.
eventmse.lbx    138  0000F      62  en             Empire have recently visited the legendary Orion star system.
eventmse.lbx    139  0000F      62  en             Empire have recently visited the legendary Orion star system.
eventmse.lbx    140  00006      62  en             Empire has defeated the Antarans in a final, glorious battle.
eventmse.lbx    141  00006      98  en             military has done what was once thought impossible: the Antarans have been completely eliminated.
eventmse.lbx    143  00022      58  en             Empire was able to completely destroy the Antaran Empire.
eventmse.lbx    148  00004      19                rebel assimilation1
eventmse.lbx    149  00004      19                rebel assimilation2
