HELP.LBX          0  00004       7                No Tech
HELP.LBX          0  0006B      14                No description
HELP.LBX          0  0057F      23  ?             Achilles Targeting Unit
HELP.LBX          0  005E6     117  en            Triples the chance of striking an enemy's weapon and shield systems and completely  bypasses the target ship's armor.
HELP.LBX          0  00AFA      16                Adamantium Armor
HELP.LBX          0  00B61     162  en            Ships with this armor have 8 times the base structure and armor points. The hit points of fighters are multiplied by 4. Adds +25 to ground troop combat strengths.
HELP.LBX          0  01075      22  ?             Advanced City Planning
HELP.LBX          0  010DC     187  en            Pre-planned, organized colony design techniques. The improvements in organization increase the maximum population that can live on all planets owned by the empire by +5 million colonists.
HELP.LBX          0  015F0      23  ?             Advanced Damage Control
HELP.LBX          0  01657     112  en            Completely repairs ships between battles. Automatically included on all ships once the technology is researched.
HELP.LBX          0  01B6B      23  ?             Alien Management Center
HELP.LBX          0  01BD2     151  en            Provides better control of occupied alien populations: aliens work harder, assimilate into your empire twice as fast, and are half as likely to revolt.
HELP.LBX          0  020E6      15                Android Farmers
HELP.LBX          0  0214D     185  en            Mechanical workers with a +3 food production bonus. Require 1 production unit per turn instead of food. They are unaffected by morale, receive no racial bonuses, and generate no income.
HELP.LBX          0  02661      18                Android Scientists
HELP.LBX          0  026C8     198  en            Mechanical workers that generate 3 research points per turn. Require 1 production unit per turn instead of food. They are unaffected by morale, receive no racial bonuses, and cannot generate income.
HELP.LBX          0  02BDC      15                Android Workers
HELP.LBX          0  02C43     184  en            Mechanical workers with a +3 production bonus. Require 1 production unit per turn instead of food. They are unaffected by morale, receive no racial bonuses, and cannot generate income.
HELP.LBX          0  03157      17  ?             Anti-Grav Harness
HELP.LBX          0  031BE     117  en            Allows ground troops and armor to fly, increasing their mobility and defense. Adds +10 to their ground combat rating.
HELP.LBX          0  036D2      15                Antimatter Bomb
HELP.LBX          0  03739     144  en            A high-yield orbital bombardment device engineered to destroy ground forces and colony installations, inflicting 5-40 points of damage per bomb.
HELP.LBX          0  03C4D      16                Antimatter Drive
HELP.LBX          0  03CB4     121  en            Capable of moving a ship 5 parsecs a turn. All ship drives are automatically upgraded when this technology is discovered.
HELP.LBX          0  041C8      21  ?             Anti-Matter Torpedoes
HELP.LBX          0  0422F     201  en            These torpedoes are balls of antimatter that explode on contact. They travel at a speed of 20 and inflict 25 points of damage and fire every other turn.  Modifications: overloaded, enveloping and ECCM.
HELP.LBX          0  04743      20  ?             Anti-Missile Rockets
HELP.LBX          0  047AA     215  en            Can only target missiles. They have a maximum range of 15 squares and will fire defensively against approaching missiles if not yet fired in that turn. The  chance to score a hit is 85% minus 5% per square distance.
HELP.LBX          0  04CBE      14                Armor Barracks
HELP.LBX          0  04D25     191  en            Creates tank battalions. It has 2 units when built, and adds 1 unit every 10 turns, up to half the planet's population. Eliminates the morale penalty for dictatorships and feudal governments.
HELP.LBX          0  05239      18  ?             Artemis System Net
HELP.LBX          0  052A0     184  en            Network of mines. Ships have a chance of damage based on size: frigate-20%, destroyer-30%, cruiser-40%, battleship-50%, titan-80%, doomstar-100%. Damage is 100-500 points less shields.
HELP.LBX          0  057B4      19                Planet Construction
HELP.LBX          0  0581B     139  en            A colony that has an asteroid field or gas giant within its star system can create a complete artificial planet capable of supporting life.
HELP.LBX          0  05D2F      16                Assault Shuttles
HELP.LBX          0  05D96     185  en            Squadron of 4 shuttles used to move 1 unit of marines each from the launching ship  onto enemy ships. They take 3 hits to destroy, modified by your best armor, and move at a speed of 6.
HELP.LBX          0  062AA      16                Astro University
HELP.LBX          0  06311     142  en            Using the most advanced teaching methods available, the efficiency of farmers, workers, and scientists is increased. Each receives a +1 bonus.
HELP.LBX          0  06825      19                Atmospheric Renewer
HELP.LBX          0  0688C     187  en            Eliminates many dangerous particles from the atmosphere of a planet. The amount of production is quartered before calculating pollution. Effects are cumulative with a pollution processor.
HELP.LBX          0  06DA0      17                Augmented Engines
HELP.LBX          0  06E07      36  ?             Increases ship's combat speed by +5.
HELP.LBX          0  0731B       7                Autolab
HELP.LBX          0  07382      71  en            A completely automated research facility. Generates 30 research points.
HELP.LBX          0  07896      19                Automated Factories
HELP.LBX          0  078FD     142  en            Aid industry workers in their building of finished products. Generates 5  production and increases the production each worker generates by +1.
HELP.LBX          0  07E11      21  ?             Automated Repair Unit
HELP.LBX          0  07E78     180  en            Repairs a ship during combat, restoring 20% of the armor or structure and 10% of the ship's internal systems each turn during combat. After combat, the ship is completely repaired.
HELP.LBX          0  0838C      10                Battleoids
HELP.LBX          0  083F3     156  en            Giant robot fighting vehicles superior in power and mobility to conventional tanks. They have a +10 bonus to their combat rating and take 3 hits to destroy.
HELP.LBX          0  08907      11                Battle Pods
HELP.LBX          0  0896E      58  en            Battle Pods increase the available space on a ship by 50%.
HELP.LBX          0  08E82      14                Battle Scanner
HELP.LBX          0  08EE9     103  en            Increases a ship's chance to hit with beam weapons by +50%. Adds +2 parsecs to galactic scanning range.
HELP.LBX          0  093FD      13                Battlestation
HELP.LBX          0  09464     138  en            Heavily armed star base, with +4 parsec scanning range bonus. Adds +10% to the offense of ships in combat around it. Replaces a star base.
HELP.LBX          0  099DF     184  en            The most advanced biochemical weapon ever devised, with a 20% chance of killing one million colonists. Use of biological weapons incurs a major diplomatic penalty with all other races.
HELP.LBX          0  09EF3      16                Biomorphic Fungi
HELP.LBX          0  09F5A     135  en            Edible plants that grow anywhere, increasing the food output of all planets by +1 food per farmer, including worlds with 0 food output.
HELP.LBX          0  0A46E      20  ?             Black Hole Generator
HELP.LBX          0  0A4D5     217  en            Creates an artificial black hole. The target ship is trapped in an intense gravity pocket and cannot move. Unless the generator or the equipped ship can be destroyed in 2 turns, the black hole will destroy the target.
HELP.LBX          0  0A9E9      11                Bomber Bays
HELP.LBX          0  0AA50     185  en            Short range ships carrying a bomb that can be dropped on a planet or detonated on a ship. They carry one bomb each of the best type available. They move in groups of 4 at a speed of 10.
HELP.LBX          0  0AF64       7                Capitol
HELP.LBX          0  0AFCB     266  en            The heart of your empire's government, the capitol is required to maintain proper order. Losing the colony that has the capitol building will have severe effects,  depending on your type of government. It can be rebuilt if destroyed,  but otherwise can not be built.
HELP.LBX          0  0B4DF      14  ?             Class I Shield
HELP.LBX          0  0B546     192  en            Protects ships from physical and energy attacks. Absorbs up to 5 times the ship's size in damage before failing, with each attack reduced by 1 point of damage. Regenerates 30% per combat turn.
HELP.LBX          0  0BA5A      16  ?             Class III Shield
HELP.LBX          0  0BAC1     194  en            Protects ships from physical and energy attacks. Absorbs up to 15 times the ship's size in damage before failing, with each attack reduced by 3 points of damage. Regenerates 30% per combat turn.
HELP.LBX          0  0BFD5      14  ?             Class V Shield
HELP.LBX          0  0C03C     194  en            Protects ships from physical and energy attacks. Absorbs up to 25 times the ship's size in damage before failing, with each attack reduced by 5 points of damage. Regenerates 30% per combat turn.
HELP.LBX          0  0C550      16  ?             Class VII Shield
HELP.LBX          0  0C5B7     193  en            Protects ships from physical and energy attacks. Absorbs up to 35 times the ship's size in damage before failing with each attack reduced by 7 points of damage. Regenerates 30% per combat turn.
HELP.LBX          0  0CACB      14  ?             Class X Shield
HELP.LBX          0  0CB32     195  en            Protects ships from physical and energy attacks. Absorbs up to 50 times the ship's size in damage before failing, with each attack reduced by 10 points of damage. Regenerates 30% per combat turn.
HELP.LBX          0  0D046      15                Cloaking Device
HELP.LBX          0  0D0AD     218  en            Completely hides a ship from long range scans. In combat, it adds +80 to the ship's beam defense and missiles have a 50% chance to miss as long as the ship does not attack. Must wait one turn without firing to recloak.
HELP.LBX          0  0D5C1      14                Cloning Center
HELP.LBX          0  0D628     170  en            Allows doctors to replace failing or damaged organs, increasing the population growth by +100K each turn as long as the current population is below the planetary maximum.
HELP.LBX          0  0DB3C      11                Colony Base
HELP.LBX          0  0DBA3      86  en            Creates a colony on another planet inside the same star system as the building colony.
HELP.LBX          0  0E0B7      11                Colony Ship
HELP.LBX          0  0E11E     152  en            Capable of creating a colony in a distant star system. Will not engage in combat and will be destroyed when attacked if not escorted by a military ship.
HELP.LBX          0  0E632      13                Confederation
HELP.LBX          0  0E699     171  en            An advanced form of feudal government on a galactic scale. Eliminates automatic assimilation into enemy empires and reduces the cost of building ships to 1/3 normal costs.
HELP.LBX          0  0EBAD      19  ?             Cyber-Security Link
HELP.LBX          0  0EC14     132  en            Provides a direct mental link to computers, allowing spies to circumvent many automated security systems. Adds +10 to all spy rolls.
HELP.LBX          0  0F128      20                Cybertronic Computer
HELP.LBX          0  0F18F     211  en            Learns and adapts using a neural net similar to the biological brain. Equipped on all ships, it adds +100% chance to hit with beam weapons.  Attack bonuses are eliminated if the computer is damaged or destroyed.
HELP.LBX          0  0F6A3      12                Damper Field
HELP.LBX          0  0F70A     222  en            Surrounds a ship with an energy dampening field that reduces the damage a ship takes by 3/4. Has a 50% chance of distorting a transporter beam attempting to move troops onto the equipped ship, killing the troops instantly.
HELP.LBX          0  0FC1E      25  ?             Dauntless Guidance System
HELP.LBX          0  0FC85     148  en            Provides friend-or-foe recognition guidance to missiles and torpedoes. They will retarget the nearest enemy ship if their first target is destroyed.
HELP.LBX          0  10199       9                Death Ray
HELP.LBX          0  10200     210  en            Fires an intense beam of cosmic rays inflicting 50-100 points of damage. Any damage that penetrates the shields kills 1 marine unit for every 5 points of internal damage. Modifications: heavy mount, continuous.
HELP.LBX          0  10714      12                Death Spores
HELP.LBX          0  1077B     227  en            Engineered viruses that attack organic lifeforms. Introduced by orbital bombardment, each launch has a 10% chance to kill one million colonists. Use of biological  weapons incurs a major diplomatic penalty with all other races.
HELP.LBX          0  10C8F      16  ?             Deep Core Mining
HELP.LBX          0  10CF6     151  en            Allows miners to build stable tunnels deep into a planet. Generates 15  production and increases the productivity of each worker by +3 production each.
HELP.LBX          0  1120A      16  ?             Core Waste Dumps
HELP.LBX          0  11271     169  en            Take man-made toxic/polluting agents and store them deep within the surface of a planet, far below surface water supplies. Planetary pollution is completely  eliminated.
HELP.LBX          0  11785      20  ?             Deuterium Fuel Cells
HELP.LBX          0  117EC      77  en            Supplies sufficient energy to propel a ship up to 6 parsecs before refueling.
HELP.LBX          0  11D00      18                Dimensional Portal
HELP.LBX          0  11D67     186  en            Allows ships to cross into the dimension of the Antaran home world. To use it, select a fleet in the same system as the portal and press the 'Attack Antarans' button on the fleet pop-up.
HELP.LBX          0  1227B      19                Displacement Device
HELP.LBX          0  122E2     126  en            All weapons targeted against an equipped ship have a 30% chance of missing completely, regardless of any other considerations.
HELP.LBX          0  127F6      16                Disrupter Cannon
HELP.LBX          0  1285D     155  en            Fires intense bolts of energy that inflict 40 points of damage. Damage from  disrupter bolts is not reduced by range. Modifications: autofire, heavy mount.
HELP.LBX          0  12D71      22  ?             Doom Star Construction
HELP.LBX          0  12DD8      69  en            Mobile planetoid bases. They are the largest ships that can be built.
HELP.LBX          0  132EC      15                Reinforced Hull
HELP.LBX          0  13353     154  en            Triples the structural integrity of a ship and provides more protection for the ship's drive system, tripling the amount of damage required to destroy it.
HELP.LBX          0  13867      10                ECM Jammer
HELP.LBX          0  138CE     132  en            Creates a magnetic pulse jamming both weapon tracking systems and missile guidance units, adding +70% to the ship's missile evasion.
HELP.LBX          0  13DE2      19                Electronic Computer
HELP.LBX          0  13E49     168  en            Directs starship weapons' fire and is automatically equipped on all ships, increasing chance to hit by +25%. This bonus is lost if the computer is damaged or destroyed.
HELP.LBX          0  1435D      25  ?             Emissions Guidance System
HELP.LBX          0  143C4     215  en            Tracks the warp signature of a vehicle. If the missile penetrates the shields, all damage is applied to the ship's drive, bypassing any armor. Requires 4 times the space and costs 4 times more than regular missiles.
HELP.LBX          0  148D8      15                Energy Absorber
HELP.LBX          0  1493F     176  en            One quarter of all damage inflicted on a ship is instead stored in the  energy absorber.  The ship must fire this stored energy at an enemy ship in the next turn or it is lost.
HELP.LBX          0  14E53      10                Biospheres
HELP.LBX          0  14EBA     185  en            Enables a colony to better control environmental conditions, allowing  colonization of the more intolerable areas of the planet. Maximum planetary population is increased by +2 million.
HELP.LBX          0  153CE      21                Evolutionary Mutation
HELP.LBX          0  15435     216  en            Allows you to mutate your race, altering their abilities. When evolutionary mutation is researched, you may choose 4 additional points of race development picks, to either remove disadvantages or increase advantages.
HELP.LBX          0  15949      19  ?             Extended Fuel Tanks
HELP.LBX          0  159B0      96  en            Increase the overall range of a ship by +50%, but at the cost of a considerable amount of space.
HELP.LBX          0  15EC4      18  ?             Fast Missile Racks
HELP.LBX          0  15F2B     168  en            Allow a ship to fire two volleys of missiles in one turn. Will only fire one per turn after that, unless the ship takes one full turn without firing missiles to reload.
HELP.LBX          0  1643F      10                Federation
HELP.LBX          0  164A6      79  en            Advanced form of Democracy. The research and income bonus is increased to +75%.
HELP.LBX          0  169BA      12                Fighter Bays
HELP.LBX          0  16A21     213  en            Allows a ship to carry a group of 4 short-range fighters. They carry one beam  weapon of the best type that can have the point defense modification, and can  fire it 4 times before returning to the launching ship.
HELP.LBX          0  16F35      16                Fighter Garrison
HELP.LBX          0  16F9C     224  en            Planetary base that houses 10-interceptors.  Fighter garrisons are equipped  with 6-bomber, or 4-heavy fighter squadrons when the appropriate technology becomes available. New fighters become available every 10 combat turns.
HELP.LBX          0  174B0      16                Food Replicators
HELP.LBX          0  17517     203  en            Alter the molecular structure of inorganic material to create edible food. Having a facility in a colony allows you to convert 2 units of production (energy) into 1 unit of food, as needed by the colony.
HELP.LBX          0  17A2B      10                Freighters
HELP.LBX          0  17A92     177  en            A group of ships to transport food or colonists as needed between worlds. Each fleet contains 5 freighters. The fleet can transport 5 food units or one population unit per turn.
HELP.LBX          0  17FA6      11                Fusion Beam
HELP.LBX          0  1800D     146  en            Projects a tetrium stream of charged particles, inflicting 2-6 points of damage Modifications: heavy mount, continuous, point defense, enveloping.
HELP.LBX          0  18521      11                Fusion Bomb
HELP.LBX          0  18588     135  en            A high-yield orbital bombardment device engineered to destroy ground forces and colony installations, inflicting 4-24 points of damage.
HELP.LBX          0  18A9C      12                Fusion Drive
HELP.LBX          0  18B03     148  en            Capable of faster than light travel, moving a ship 3 parsecs a turn. All ship  drives are automatically upgraded when this technology is discovered.
HELP.LBX          0  19017      12                Fusion Rifle
HELP.LBX          0  1907E     144  en            A powerful hand-held rifle that increases the combat rating of militia, troops, and armor by +10. The bonus is not cumulative with other rifles.
HELP.LBX          0  19592      19                Gaia Transformation
HELP.LBX          0  195F9     174  en            Creates an environment suited to both plant and animal growth by introducing genetically-engineered microorganisms into the world. Can only be applied to terran environments.
HELP.LBX          0  19B0D      26  ?             Galactic Currency Exchange
HELP.LBX          0  19B74     147  en            Eliminates the need for hard currency, replacing it with instantaneous electronic exchanges. Increases the money generated by all colonies by +50%.
HELP.LBX          0  1A088      17                Galactic Cybernet
HELP.LBX          0  1A0EF     187  en            Nearly instantaneous galaxy-wide communications, allowing quick exchange of information and ideas. The cybernet generates 15 research points and each scientist generates +3 research each.
HELP.LBX          0  1A603      20                Galactic Unification
HELP.LBX          0  1A66A     214  en            Connects all beings within the race in a collective consciousness, allowing each to act in total harmony.  Farmer and worker production is increased by +100%. Only races that began with unification can research it.
HELP.LBX          0  1AB7E      12                Gauss Cannon
HELP.LBX          0  1ABE5     150  en            An extremely powerful linear accelerator which inflicts 18 points of damage regardless of range. Modifications: autofire, armor piercing, heavy mount.
HELP.LBX          0  1B0F9      13                Graviton Beam
HELP.LBX          0  1B160     188  en            Gravitic waves that tear a target apart. Inflicts 3-15 points of damage. Any damage penetrating the ship's shields inflicts extra structural damage. Modifications: heavy mount, continuous.
HELP.LBX          0  1B674      17                Gyro Destabilizer
HELP.LBX          0  1B6DB     219  en            Creates a sudden rift in a ship's subspace field. Weakens the inertial controls of the ship, spinning it in random directions, inflicting 1-4 points of structural damage times the ship's size class. Range is 15 squares.
HELP.LBX          0  1BBEF      12                Hard Shields
HELP.LBX          0  1BC56     220  en            Reduces the damage of any attack by an additional 3 points. Allows operation of all shields in a nebula and prevents the use of enemy transporters even after  shields have been dropped. Immune to shield-piercing weapons.
HELP.LBX          0  1C16A      11                Heavy Armor
HELP.LBX          0  1C1D1     130  en            Heavy armor negates armor piercing effects and reinforces the armor of a ship, tripling the amount of damage the armor can absorb.
HELP.LBX          0  1C6E5      18  ?             Heavy Fighter Bays
HELP.LBX          0  1C74C     195  en            Allow ships to carry heavy fighters equipped with 2 of the best point defense  beam weapons and 2 of the best bombs available. They have 5 hits, modified by your best armor, and move at speed 12.
HELP.LBX          0  1CC60      23                Heightened Intelligence
HELP.LBX          0  1CCC7     148  en            Through genetic engineering, the average intelligence of the entire race is substantially improved, increasing the research of all scientists by +1.
HELP.LBX          0  1D1DB      17  ?             High Energy Focus
HELP.LBX          0  1D242     190  en            Allows a ship to channel the fire of its energy weapons more efficiently, increasing damage by +50% over base regardless of range. It does not improve the chances of hitting distant targets.
HELP.LBX          0  1D756      14                Holo Simulator
HELP.LBX          0  1D7BD     107  en            Capable of creating realistic 3-D images from holographic projections. Increases a planet's morale by +20%.
HELP.LBX          0  1DCD1      16                Hydroponic Farms
HELP.LBX          0  1DD38     137  en            An automated, sealed environment in which food can be grown, even on lifeless worlds. It increases the food output of a world by +2 food.
HELP.LBX          0  1E24C      11                Hyper Drive
HELP.LBX          0  1E2B3     122  en            Capable of moving a ship 6 parsecs a turn. All ship drives are automatically  upgraded when this technology is discovered.
HELP.LBX          0  1E7C7      11                Megafluxers
HELP.LBX          0  1E82E     214  en            Conduct and magnify energy transmission in less space, giving a ship more space for equipment. Increases the amount of equipment it can carry by +25%. Megafluxers  are used automatically on all ships once acquired.
HELP.LBX          0  1ED42      18  ?             Hyper-X Capacitors
HELP.LBX          0  1EDA9     171  en            Allow ship beam weapons to fire twice in a turn. After firing twice, one turn must be spent without firing beam weapons; otherwise the weapons can only fire once per turn.
HELP.LBX          0  1F2BD      25                Hyperspace Communications
HELP.LBX          0  1F324     189  en            Allow you to communicate with any ship already in hyperspace so you can change its destination. Increases the command points of star bases, battle stations and star fortresses by +3 points.
HELP.LBX          0  1F838       8                Imperium
HELP.LBX          0  1F89F     123  en            Advanced form of dictatorship. Total command points generated are increased by +50% and all defensive spy rolls are at +20.
HELP.LBX          0  1FDB3      18                Inertial Nullifier
HELP.LBX          0  1FE1A     204  en            Creates a warp field that can operate in normal space. Increases ship mobility and makes it harder to target. Adds +100 to the ship's beam defense, and allows it to change direction without movement cost.
HELP.LBX          0  2032E      19                Inertial Stabilizer
HELP.LBX          0  20395     219  en            Creates a partial warp field that can operate in normal space. It vastly  improves the ship's mobility and makes it considerably harder to target, adding +50 to ship's beam defense and halving movement cost for turning.
HELP.LBX          0  208A9      17                Interphased Drive
HELP.LBX          0  20910     122  en            Capable of moving a ship 7 parsecs a turn. All ship drives are automatically  upgraded when this technology is discovered.
HELP.LBX          0  20E24       9                Ion Drive
HELP.LBX          0  20E8B     122  en            Capable of moving a ship 4 parsecs a turn. All ship drives are automatically  upgraded when this technology is discovered.
HELP.LBX          0  2139F      16  ?             Ion Pulse Cannon
HELP.LBX          0  21406     224  en            Fires a particle wave that overloads ships' systems and inflicts 2-10 points of  damage, bypassing all armor and structure. Completely ineffective against  monsters and Antaran ships. Modifications: autofire, and continuous.
HELP.LBX          0  2191A      19  ?             Irridium Fuel Cells
HELP.LBX          0  21981      71  en            Supplies sufficient energy to propel a ship 9 parsecs before refueling.
HELP.LBX          0  21E95       9                Jump Gate
HELP.LBX          0  21EFC     187  en            Forms a controlled wormhole between two points, increasing the speed of ships moving through it by 3 parsecs a turn. Once discovered, all colonies will automatically be equipped with one.
HELP.LBX          0  22410      12                Laser Cannon
HELP.LBX          0  22477     178  en            Highly focused, coherent beams of light which deliver 1-4 points of damage. Modifications: autofire, armor piercing, heavy mount, continuous, point defense, no range dissipation.
HELP.LBX          0  2298B      11                Laser Rifle
HELP.LBX          0  229F2     135  en            A hand-held weapon that increases the combat rating of militia, troops, and armor by +5. The bonus is not cumulative with other rifles.
HELP.LBX          0  22F06      15                Lightning Field
HELP.LBX          0  22F6D     200  en            Surrounds a ship in a powerful energized field capable of overloading the targeting system of any missile, torpedo or fighter. Has a 50% chance of destroying these weapons before they damage the ship.
HELP.LBX          0  23481      15                Marine Barracks
HELP.LBX          0  234E8     231  en            Lets the colony train troops for ground invasion protection. Begins with 4 marine units, then trains 1 unit every 5 turns, up to the planet's maximum population. Eliminates morale penalties for dictatorships and feudal governments.
HELP.LBX          0  239FC      11                Mass Driver
HELP.LBX          0  23A63     176  en            A rail gun firing a hyper-velocity projectile. Inflicts 6 points of damage. Damage is not reduced by range. Modifications: autofire, armor piercing, heavy mount, point defense.
HELP.LBX          0  23F77      13                Mauler Device
HELP.LBX          0  23FDE     157  en            Fires a bolt of pure energy that always hits. Inflicts 100 points of damage, but with double the range penalties for dissipation. Modifications: heavy mount.
HELP.LBX          0  244F2      17                Merculite Missile
HELP.LBX          0  24559     163  en            Carries a powerful, chemically-based explosive warhead capable of delivering 14 points of damage. Modifications: MIRV, emissions guidance, fast, armored, and ECCM.
HELP.LBX          0  24A6D      12                Microbiotics
HELP.LBX          0  24AD4     185  en            Microorganisms used to create drugs. Increases the population growth rate of all planets by +25% and halves the percentage chance for death spores and bio-terminators to kill colonists.
HELP.LBX          0  24FE8      22                Microlite Construction
HELP.LBX          0  2504F     179  en            Uses microscopic nano-machines to construct buildings and ships with less metal, but with the same strength and durability. Increases productivity of all workers by +1 production.
HELP.LBX          0  25563      12                Outpost Ship
HELP.LBX          0  255CA     220  en            Capable of creating an outpost on any uninhabited planet. Outposts function like a colony, except no population units may be moved there. Outpost ships are unarmed and will be destroyed if not escorted by military ships.
HELP.LBX          0  25ADE      24                Moleculartronic Computer
HELP.LBX          0  25B45     124  en            Directs all starship weapon fire, adding +125% to the chance to hit. If the computer is destroyed, the ship loses the bonus.
HELP.LBX          0  26059      21  ?             Multi-Wave ECM Jammer
HELP.LBX          0  260C0     105  en            Jamming frequencies across the entire spectrum this device adds +100 to the ships missile evasion rating.
HELP.LBX          0  265D4      20  ?             Multi-Phased Shields
HELP.LBX          0  2663B     102  en            Allow ships to rapidly change the frequency of their shields, increasing the maximum strength by +50%.
HELP.LBX          0  26B4F      18                Nano Disassemblers
HELP.LBX          0  26BB6     171  en            Microscopic nano-machines capable of breaking down environmental contaminants. Doubles the number of production units a planet can produce before any pollution is created.
HELP.LBX          0  270CA      14                Neural Scanner
HELP.LBX          0  27131     195  en            With improved data processing methods, the pathways of the brain can be mapped and analyzed. Provides a near perfect lie detector used by spies to elicit information, adding +10 to all spy rolls.
HELP.LBX          0  27645      15                Neutron Blaster
HELP.LBX          0  276AC     223  en            Fires an intense beam of lethal radiation. Inflicts 3-12 points of damage to shields. Any damage that penetrates the shields kills 1 marine unit for every 5 points of internal damage. Modifications: heavy mount, continuous.
HELP.LBX          0  27BC0      15                Neutron Scanner
HELP.LBX          0  27C27     206  en            Detects enemy ships. Has a base detection range of 5 parsecs. Ships in transit can be detected at 1 parsec per size class of ship greater range. Neutron scanners  reduce enemy ship's missile evasion by -40.
HELP.LBX          0  2813B      16                Neutronium Armor
HELP.LBX          0  281A2     162  en            Ships with this armor have 6 times the base structure and armor points. The hit points of fighters are multiplied by 5. Adds +20 to ground troop combat strengths.
HELP.LBX          0  286B6      15                Neutronium Bomb
HELP.LBX          0  2871D     136  en            A high-yield orbital bombardment device engineered to destroy ground forces and colony installations, inflicting 10-60 points of damage.
HELP.LBX          0  28C31      12                Nuclear Bomb
HELP.LBX          0  28C98     135  en            A high-yield orbital bombardment device engineered to destroy ground forces and colony installations, inflicting 3-12 points of damage.
HELP.LBX          0  291AC      13                Nuclear Drive
HELP.LBX          0  29213     114  en            Capable of moving a ship 2 parsecs per turn. This is the first ship drive that makes interstellar travel possible.
HELP.LBX          0  29727      15                Nuclear Missile
HELP.LBX          0  2978E     144  en            Carries a high-yield nuclear warhead that inflicts 8 points of damage.  Modifications: MIRV, emissions guidance, fast, heavily armored and ECCM.
HELP.LBX          0  29CA2      17                Optronic Computer
HELP.LBX          0  29D09     111  en            Directs all starship weapons fire, adding +50 to the chance to hit. Bonus is lost if the computer is destroyed.
HELP.LBX          0  2A21D      13                Particle Beam
HELP.LBX          0  2A284     181  en            Fires a stream of matter in a focused energy beam that is naturally shield piercing,  and inflicts 10-30 points of damage. Modifications: continous, heavy mount, and  point defense.
HELP.LBX          0  2A798      15                Personal Shield
HELP.LBX          0  2A7FF     103  en            Deflects physical and energy attacks, increasing the combat rating of militia, troops and armor by +20.
HELP.LBX          0  2AD13      13                Phase Shifter
HELP.LBX          0  2AD7A     124  en            A derivative of a subspace teleporter that allows the equipped ship to teleport itself or another ship 18 squares in combat.
HELP.LBX          0  2B28E      13                Phasing Cloak
HELP.LBX          0  2B2F5     237  en            Allows a ship to temporarily enter another dimension instead of just visually disappearing. While cloaked, the ship cannot be detected or attacked. Can only function for 10 turns, after which it will act like an ordinary cloaking device.
HELP.LBX          0  2B809       6                Phasor
HELP.LBX          0  2B870     215  en            Fires a trans-warp beam of phased energy that actually exists in several dimensions simultaneously, inflicting 5-20 points of damage. Modifications: autofire, continuous, heavy mount, point defense, shield piercing.
HELP.LBX          0  2BD84      12                Phasor Rifle
HELP.LBX          0  2BDEB     187  en            A hand held rifle that can almost disintegrate an opponent with one blast, increasing the combat rating of militia, troops and armor by +20. The bonus is not cumulative with other rifles.
HELP.LBX          0  2C2FF      24  ?             Planetary Barrier Shield
HELP.LBX          0  2C366     177  en            Seals a planet in an energy field. Converts Radiated climates to Barren climates. Reduces damage against a planet by 20 points. Ground troops and biological weapons cannot pass.
HELP.LBX          0  2C87A      21  ?             Planetary Flux Shield
HELP.LBX          0  2C8E1     175  en            Seals planet in an energy field. Converts Radiated climates into Barren. Reduces damage against the planet 10 points. It replaces any planetary radiation shield already built.
HELP.LBX          0  2CDF5      27  ?             Planetary Gravity Generator
HELP.LBX          0  2CE5C     159  en            Creates artificial gravity to normalize a planet to standard gravity limits. Gravity generators eliminate the negative effects of low and heavy gravity fields.
HELP.LBX          0  2D370      22  ?             Planetary Missile Base
HELP.LBX          0  2D3D7      68  en            Contains 300 space units of your best missiles, with unlimited ammo.
HELP.LBX          0  2D8EB      16                Ground Batteries
HELP.LBX          0  2D952     128  en            Ground installation that contains 300 space units of heavy mount and point defense  versions of the best available beam weapons.
HELP.LBX          0  2DE66      26  ?             Planetary Radiation Shield
HELP.LBX          0  2DECD     168  en            Reduces solar and cosmic bombardment so lifeforms can comfortably move about the surface. Radiated climates become Barren.  Reduces damage against a planet by 5 points.
HELP.LBX          0  2E3E1      24  ?             Planetary Stock Exchange
HELP.LBX          0  2E448      51  en            Increases the revenues earned on a planet by +100%.
HELP.LBX          0  2E95C      23                Planetary Supercomputer
HELP.LBX          0  2E9C3     143  en            Supplies researchers with a vast amount of information. Generates 10 research  points and increases the research each scientist produces by +2.
HELP.LBX          0  2EED7      13                Plasma Cannon
HELP.LBX          0  2EF3E     214  en            Fires a blast of plasma energy inflicting 6-30 points of damage to all 4 shields of  the target. Only focuses well over a short range, doubling all range penalties.  Modifications: heavy mount, and continuous fire.
HELP.LBX          0  2F452      12                Plasma Rifle
HELP.LBX          0  2F4B9     151  en            The most powerful held weapon, increasing the combat rating of militia, troops, and armor by +30. The bonus is not cumulative with other rifle bonuses.
HELP.LBX          0  2F9CD      16                Plasma Torpedoes
HELP.LBX          0  2FA34     232  en            Plasma warhead capable of 120 points of damage. Travels with a combat speed of 24, losing 5 points of strength for each square traveled and firing every other turn.  Modifications: overloaded, enveloping, ECCM, no range dissipation.
HELP.LBX          0  2FF48      10                Plasma Web
HELP.LBX          0  2FFAF     172  en            An energy web that envelopes a target within a 15 square range. Inflicts 5-25  points of damage per turn. This damage persists, dissipating at a rate of  5 points per turn.
HELP.LBX          0  304C3      13                Pleasure Dome
HELP.LBX          0  3052A     176  en            The ultimate in virtual holographic entertainment, creating completely immersive entertainment environments. It increases morale by +30% and is  cumulative with holo simulator.
HELP.LBX          0  30A3E      26  ?             Pollution Control Facility
HELP.LBX          0  30AA5     128  en            Uses advanced chemicals to process factory waste. Only half of  the actual production of the planet used to calculate pollution.
HELP.LBX          0  30FB9      19                Positronic Computer
HELP.LBX          0  31020     139  en            Directs all ship beam weapons fire, adding a +75% chance to hit.  If the computer is damaged or destroyed, the ship loses the attack bonus.
HELP.LBX          0  31534      13                Powered Armor
HELP.LBX          0  3159B     195  en            Provides troops with superior power and mobility by mechanically magnifying their natural strength. Powered armor equipped troops have a +10 bonus to their combat rating and take +1 hits to kill.
HELP.LBX          0  31AAF      11                Pulse Rifle
HELP.LBX          0  31B16      54  en            Hand-held weapon that fires high-velocity projectiles.
HELP.LBX          0  3202A      16                Proton Torpedoes
HELP.LBX          0  32091     238  en            Energy projectiles traveling at trans-warp speed, striking their target the turn they are fired. They inflict 40 points of damage. Can be fired every other turn, with a max range of 24 squares. Modifications: overloaded, enveloping, ECCM.
HELP.LBX          0  325A5       8                Psionics
HELP.LBX          0  3260C     172  en            Allows you to create psychic beings of immense power. Spying bonuses are raised by +10. Morale on all planets is increased by 10% for dictatorships and imperium government.
HELP.LBX          0  32B20       6                Pulsar
HELP.LBX          0  32B87     168  en            When fired, causes violent vibrations in ships, missiles and fighters adjacent to the equipped ships. Inflicts 2-24 points of damage per size class of the ship damaged.
HELP.LBX          0  3309B      14                Pulson Missile
HELP.LBX          0  33102     145  en            Carries a powerful high-energy pulse capable of delivering 20 points of damage. Modifications: MIRV, emissions guidance, fast, armored, and ECCM.
HELP.LBX          0  33616      17                Quantum Detonator
HELP.LBX          0  3367D     224  en            Creates an interphase reaction when the ship is destroyed or self destructs, tripling the destructive power of the ship's explosion.  Ships equipped with  a quantum detonator have a 50% chance to self-destruct when captured.
HELP.LBX          0  33B91      16                Rangemaster Unit
HELP.LBX          0  33BF8     122  en            Corrects for long-range targeting inaccuracies, the actual range is  divided by three for purposes of to-hit bonuses only.
HELP.LBX          0  3410C      11                Recyclotron
HELP.LBX          0  34173     174  en            Allows scrap material reuse, reducing construction costs. Every unit of population generates +1 production. This increase does not count toward the planetary pollution level.
HELP.LBX          0  34687      16                Reflection Field
HELP.LBX          0  346EE     195  en            Subspace field that reflects beam weapons back on the attacker. Chance to reflect is the ratio of reflection field strength of 10 to the sum of weapon attack damage and reflection field strength.
HELP.LBX          0  34C02      15                Robotic Factory
HELP.LBX          0  34C69     107  en            Builds mechanical workers that add production dependent on a colony's mineral resources 5, 8, 10, 15 or 20.
HELP.LBX          0  3517D      19                Research Laboratory
HELP.LBX          0  351E4     172  en            Houses state-of-the-art computer equipment, creating a superior research environment. Generates 5 research points and increases the research each  scientist produces by +1.
HELP.LBX          0  3575F     163  en            Automate many difficult tasks, increasing the productivity of industrial workers. Generates 10 production and increases the production each worker  produces by +2.
HELP.LBX          0  35C73      13                Space Scanner
HELP.LBX          0  35CDA     129  en            Detects enemy ships. Base detection range is 1 parsec. Ships in transit can  be detected 1 parsec further per size class of ship.
HELP.LBX          0  361EE       9                Scout Lab
HELP.LBX          0  36255     223  en            A computer assisted laboratory that generates an amount of research dependent on ship size: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, or 32. Also adds +10 per size class to the attack roll of all ships in a fleet fighting space monsters or Antarans.
HELP.LBX          0  36769      17                Security Stations
HELP.LBX          0  367D0     192  en            Automatically controls and monitors vital sections of ship, attacking intruders with computer-controlled weapons. Adds +20 to the combat rolls of marines when defending against enemy boarders.
HELP.LBX          0  36CE4       7                Sensors
HELP.LBX          0  36D4B     189  en            Detects enemy ships. Has a base detection range of 8 parsecs.  Ships in transit can be detected 1 parsec further per size class of ship. Sensors reduce enemy  ship's missile evasion by -70.
HELP.LBX          0  3725F      17                Shield Capacitors
HELP.LBX          0  372C6      78  en            Increases the recharge rate of ship shields by +70% of their maximum strength.
HELP.LBX          0  377DA      15                Soil Enrichment
HELP.LBX          0  37841     197  en            Using nano-machines, planetary soil can be molecularly enriched and fertilized, increasing the food a farmer can harvest by +1. Soil enrichment will not work in barren, radiated, and toxic planets.
HELP.LBX          0  37D55      13                Space Academy
HELP.LBX          0  37DBC     111  en            Trains ship crews, adding 1 to their starting level. Ships stationed in the system gain 2 experience each turn.
HELP.LBX          0  382D0       9                Spaceport
HELP.LBX          0  38337      86  en            Site for commercial transactions, increasing the money generation of a colony by +50%.
HELP.LBX          0  3884B      18                Spatial Compressor
HELP.LBX          0  388B2     184  en            Creates an instantaneous subspace distortion in a 2-square radius about the equipped ship.  Everything in the area sustains 4-32 structural hits times its size class, ignoring shields.
HELP.LBX          0  38DC6      12                Spy Networks
HELP.LBX          0  38E2D     137  en            Trains a number of spies that you can either use as defensive agents or active spies to steal technology or sabotage enemy installations.
HELP.LBX          0  39341      19  ?             Standard Fuel Cells
HELP.LBX          0  393A8      71  en            Supplies sufficient energy to propel a ship 4 parsecs before refueling.
HELP.LBX          0  398BC       9                Star Base
HELP.LBX          0  39923     223  en            Armed orbital platforms used to service military ships.  They are equipped with extensive weaponry, the best available scanner with a +2 scanning range bonus and a star dock capable of building ships larger than destroyers.
HELP.LBX          0  39E37      13                Star Fortress
HELP.LBX          0  39E9E     187  en            A large military orbital platform. Has a +6 parsec scan range bonus and adds +20% to both the offense and defense of all ships in combat around it. Replaces battlestations and star bases.
HELP.LBX          0  3A3B2       9                Star Gate
HELP.LBX          0  3A419     143  en            Allows instantaneous movement between any of your colonies. All colonies are automatically equipped with one once the technology is researched.
HELP.LBX          0  3A92D      12                Stasis Field
HELP.LBX          0  3A994     202  en            Places target in suspended animation. It cannot fire, recharge weapons, cloak or be attacked. Field has a 3-square range and will hold the  target ship until the stasis field is turned off or destroyed.
HELP.LBX          0  3AEA8      13                Stealth Field
HELP.LBX          0  3AF0F     135  en            Reduces the gravitic emissions from FTL drives. Ships equipped with stealth fields can not be detected at any range on the main screen.
HELP.LBX          0  3B423      12                Stealth Suit
HELP.LBX          0  3B48A     102  en            Renders a person virtually invisible, blending the wearer into the background. Adds +10 all spy rolls.
HELP.LBX          0  3B99E      17                Stellar Converter
HELP.LBX          0  3BA05     215  en            A plasma cannon that can be mounted on a ship or a planet. Automatically inflicts 400 hits to all shields of any ship, regardless of range and defense. Completely destroys a planet when used for orbital bombardment.
HELP.LBX          0  3BF19      19                Structural Analyzer
HELP.LBX          0  3BF80     143  en            Links to ship's weapons array to more accurately choose target's weak armor points. All damage that penetrates the target's shields is doubled.
HELP.LBX          0  3C494      23                Subspace Communications
HELP.LBX          0  3C4FB     181  en            Allows you to issue orders to any ship within 6 squares of a star system with a starbase, battlestation, or star fortress. Increases the command points given by a base by +2 points.
HELP.LBX          0  3CA0F      19                Subspace Teleporter
HELP.LBX          0  3CA76     152  en            Allows a ship to execute a hyperspace jump of up to 20 squares. The jump does not change the ship's direction; it must rotate normally to change facing.
HELP.LBX          0  3CF8A      18                Subterranean Farms
HELP.LBX          0  3CFF1      93  en            An underground cavern system of automated farms. Increases the food output of a planet by +4.
HELP.LBX          0  3D505      13                Survival Pods
HELP.LBX          0  3D56C     175  en            Provide suspended animation facilities for legendary officers if their ship is destroyed. At least one friendly ship must survive the combat to rescue any  surviving officers.
HELP.LBX          0  3DA80      22                Tachyon Communications
HELP.LBX          0  3DAE7     206  en            Integrated into star bases, battlestations and star fortresses. Emits  signals which penetrate hyperspace. Ships within 3 parsecs can receive your orders.  Increases the command points of these bases by +1.
HELP.LBX          0  3DFFB      15                Tachyon Scanner
HELP.LBX          0  3E062     196  en            Detect enemy ships. Has a base detection range of 3 parsecs. Ships in transit  can be detected 1 parsec further per size class of ship. Tachyon scanners reduce enemy ship's missile evasion by -20.
HELP.LBX          0  3E576      19                Telepathic Training
HELP.LBX          0  3E5DD     196  en            Develops the talents of naturally telepathic members of your race. Enables you to form a more effective police force with an ability to get at the truth in a new way. Adds +5% to all spying rolls.
HELP.LBX          0  3EAF1      12                Terraforming
HELP.LBX          0  3EB58     202  en            Makes a planet more hospitable. Barren becomes desert or tundra, deserts become arid, tundras become swamp, oceans, swamps and arid become terran. Each use on  a planet increases cost by 250 production.
HELP.LBX          0  3F06C      18  ?             Thorium Fuel Cells
HELP.LBX          0  3F0D3     104  en            Advanced fuel system that self-regenerates, providing all ships with an unlimited fuel supply and range.
HELP.LBX          0  3F5E7      21  ?             Time Warp Facilitator
HELP.LBX          0  3F64E     134  en            Allows a ship to shift in and out of the time-space continuum, enabling it to take an additional turn at the end of every combat turn.
HELP.LBX          0  3FB62      18                Titan Construction
HELP.LBX          0  3FBC9     160  en            The titan class of starship is gigantic in proportion to other ships, and requires advanced engineering techniques to both construct and integrate ship systems.
HELP.LBX          0  400DD      14                Titanium Armor
HELP.LBX          0  40144      28  en            The standard armor of ships.
HELP.LBX          0  40658      12                Tractor Beam
HELP.LBX          0  406BF     204  en            It requires 1 tractor beam per size class of target ship to completely stop  the target. Ships not held completely lose a portion of movement. Motionless  ships can be boarded and are easy targets to hit.
HELP.LBX          0  40BD3       9                Transport
HELP.LBX          0  40C3A     236  en            Troop carrier for landing 4 marine units on a planet. They do not engage in combat and will be destroyed when attacked if not escorted by military ships. Once used, they are dismantled. Can only be built on planets with marine barracks.
HELP.LBX          0  4114E      12                Transporters
HELP.LBX          0  411B5     183  en            Allow a ship to move marines to an enemy ship at a range of 12 squares, as long as the shield facing the ship is down. Can also be used to drop bombs on planets up to 12 squares away.
HELP.LBX          0  416C9      15                Tritanium Armor
HELP.LBX          0  41730     162  en            Ships with this armor have twice the base structure and armor points. The hit points of fighters are multiplied by 1.5. Adds +10 to ground troop combat strengths.
HELP.LBX          0  41C44      10                Troop Pods
HELP.LBX          0  41CAB     170  en            Troop pods house additional detachments of space marines, doubling the number of marines on board a ship. The additional marines can defend the ship or board enemy ships.
HELP.LBX          0  421BF      18                Universal Antidote
HELP.LBX          0  42226     178  en            Increases the population growth rate of all colonies by +50% and quarters the chance for death spores and bio-terminators to kill a population.  Not cumulative with microbiotics.
HELP.LBX          0  4273A      19  ?             Urridium Fuel Cells
HELP.LBX          0  427A1      70  en            Supply sufficient energy to propel a ship 12 parsecs before refueling.
HELP.LBX          0  42CB5      23  ?             Virtual Reality Network
HELP.LBX          0  42D1C     162  en            Creates a galaxy wide cyberspace connection which individuals can tap into to experience alternate realities. Increases morale +20% throughout your entire empire.
HELP.LBX          0  43230      15                Warp Dissipator
HELP.LBX          0  43297     159  en            Creates a large radius field about a ship that prevents any ship from entering into hyperspace. Enemy ships cannot retreat while the dissipator is functioning.
HELP.LBX          0  437AB      16                Warp Interdictor
HELP.LBX          0  43812     186  en            Creates a warp destabilizing field around the star system in which it is built. Generates a field 2 parsecs in radius about the system that slows all enemy movement to 1 parsec per turn.
HELP.LBX          0  43D26      22  ?             Weather Control System
HELP.LBX          0  43D8D     128  en            Modifies a planet's weather patterns to create a more stable farming environment. Food production is increased by +2 per farmer.
HELP.LBX          0  442A1      16  ?             Wide Area Jammer
HELP.LBX          0  44308     231  en            Adds +130 to a ship's missile evasion rating, adds +70 to the missile evasion of other ships in the fleet. The fleet's bonus is not  cumulative with any missile evasion bonus given by other jammers. Only the best  bonus will apply.
HELP.LBX          0  4481C      15                Xeno Psychology
HELP.LBX          0  44883     190  en            Focuses on the motivations of other races in an attempt to form deals that are more appealing. The effect is to permanently add +30 diplomatic points to every deal offered to your opponents.
HELP.LBX          0  44D97      16                Xentronium Armor
HELP.LBX          0  44DFE     163  en            Ships with this armor have 10 times the base structure and armor points. The hit points of fighters are multiplied by 5. Adds +30 to ground troop combat strengths.
HELP.LBX          0  45312      12                Zeon Missile
HELP.LBX          0  45379     154  en            Carries a powerful explosive warhead capable of delivering 30 points of damage. Modifications: MIRV, emissions guidance, fast traveling, armored and ECCM.
HELP.LBX          0  4588D      14                Zortrium Armor
HELP.LBX          0  458F4     162  en            Ships with this armor have 4 times the base structure and armor points. The hit points of fighters are multiplied by 2. Adds +15 to ground troop combat strengths.
HELP.LBX          0  45E08      13                Hyper Biology
HELP.LBX          0  45E6F     138  en            Hyper advances in Biology serve to increase the miniaturization levels of all genetics applications and are worth +5 points to your score.
HELP.LBX          0  46383      11                Hyper Power
HELP.LBX          0  463EA     133  en            Hyper advances in Power serve to increase the miniaturization levels of all power applications and are worth +5 points to your score.
HELP.LBX          0  468FE      13                Hyper Physics
HELP.LBX          0  46965     137  en            Hyper advances in Physics serve to increase the miniaturization levels of all physics applications and are worth +5 points to your score.
HELP.LBX          0  46E79      18                Hyper Construction
HELP.LBX          0  46EE0     147  en            Hyper advances in Construction serve to increase the miniaturization levels of all construction applications and are worth +5 points to your score.
HELP.LBX          0  473F4      12                Hyper Fields
HELP.LBX          0  4745B     135  en            Hyper advances in Fields serve to increase the miniaturization levels of all fields applications and are worth +5 points to your score.
HELP.LBX          0  4796F      15                Hyper Chemistry
HELP.LBX          0  479D6     141  en            Hyper advances in Chemistry serve to increase the miniaturization levels of all chemistry applications and are worth +5 points to your score.
HELP.LBX          0  47EEA      15                Hyper Computers
HELP.LBX          0  47F51     140  en            Hyper advances in Computers serve to increase the miniaturization levels of all computer applications and are worth +5 points to your score.
HELP.LBX          0  48465      15                Hyper Sociology
HELP.LBX          0  484CC     141  en            Hyper advances in Sociology serve to increase the miniaturization levels of all sociology applications and are worth +5 points to your score.
HELP.LBX          0  489E0      19  ?             Create New Colonies
HELP.LBX          0  48A47     693  en            If you want to create a new colony within the same system as a colony you  already own, choose to build a COLONY BASE from the Colony Production screen.  Once built, you will be asked to select the planet you wish to place it on.  One unit of the building colony's population is also transfered to the new  colony. To create a colony in a new star system, choose to build a COLONY  SHIP. When done, the building colony transfers one population unit to the  ship, which can then be sent to a new system. Once it arrives, you will be  prompted to select a planet to land on. Colony ships can be moved like any  other ship, or can be sent using the SEND COLONY SHIP button on the  Planets screen.
HELP.LBX          0  48F5B      10                Move Ships
HELP.LBX          0  48FC2     653  en            To move a ship from one system to another, click on its icon on the main  Galaxy Map.  This will display all ships currently in orbit around that  system. All ships highlighted in blue are currently selected. Clicking on  individual pictures selects/deselects them, clicking on ALL  selects/deselects all ships in that fleet. Once you have highlighted the  ships you wish to move, move the cursor over the star system to wish to send  them to. A green line indicates that it is within range, and the popup lists  the ETA in turns. If the line is red, the system is out of range. The popup  indicates how many parsecs away it is from your nearest colony.
HELP.LBX          0  494D6      14                Move Colonists
HELP.LBX          0  4953D     719  en            There are two ways to transfer colonists. You can select the colony you wish to transfer from, then click on the population unit you wish to move. A TRANSFER COLONISTS button will appear. Clicking on this button brings up a list of your colonies, with icons representing their current population. Place the colonist you selected in the box corresponding to the colony you are sending it to. You can also transfer colonists by clicking on the COLONIES button on the main Galaxy Map screen. Select the unit of population you wish to move, and put in the appropriate occupation box of the colony you wish to move it to. In both cases, you will receive a warning if the colony you selected is already at maximum population.
HELP.LBX          0  49A51      14                Assign Leaders
HELP.LBX          0  49AB8     342  en            To assign a leader to a planet or ship, click on the LEADERS button on either the main Galaxy Map screen or on the Colony screen. You can toggle between colony leaders and ship officers by  clicking on the buttons in the top left corner. Select the ship or star system you wish to assign a leader to, then select which leader you are sending.
HELP.LBX          0  49FCC      13  en            Go to Antares
HELP.LBX          0  4A033     328  en            First you must build a Dimensional Portal. If you are not a trans-dimensional race, you can research this application under Multi-Dimensional Physics. Once a colony has built the portal, click on the ships orbiting that colony that you wish to send. An ATTACK ANTARES button will appear; selecting it sends the fleet to Antares.
HELP.LBX          0  4A547      14                Invade Planets
HELP.LBX          0  4A5AE     549  en            You must have a TRANSPORT SHIP in your fleet to capture a planet. Send the fleet to the system and select the planet you wish to capture. If you lose the combat, your transport ships will retreat. If you win, you will be promted to either BOMBARD or INVADE. You can choose to bombard slowly, then stop and invade after the colony's defenses have been destroyed. If your invasion is sucessful, you can elect to annihilate the occupants, or force them to serve you. Specific race characteristics and technologies will affect your ability to do either.
HELP.LBX          0  4AAC2      13                Capture Ships
HELP.LBX          0  4AB29     369  en            You must have a ship equipped with TRANSPORTERS to capture a ship. Transporters allow a ship to move marines to an enemy ship at a range of 12 squares, as long as the enemy's shield facing the ship is down. Once the transportes reach the enemy, a quick combat occurs. If you are sucessful, the enemy ship is taken over, and becomes yours at the end of the space combat.
HELP.LBX          0  4B03D      16  ?             Change Tax Rates
HELP.LBX          0  4B0A4     241  en            Left click on the TREASURY WINDOW on the main Galaxy Map screen. This brings up a popup from which you can set your new rate. The percentage value of the tax rate is the percentage of all production from your colonies to be turned into cash.
HELP.LBX          0  4B5B8      18                Prevent Supernovas
HELP.LBX          0  4B61F     360  en            If threat of a supernova occurs in one of your star systems, you need to maximize research within that system. The total number of research points generated by all colonies in the system are applied to research on a solar regenerator. If your total accumulated research points exceeds the strength of the supernova before time is up, the disaster is prevented.
HELP.LBX          0  4BB33      13  en            Cure a Plague
HELP.LBX          0  4BB9A     295  en            Once a plague occurs on one of your colonies, you need to maximize the amount of research being done in that colony. All research points generated in that colony are applied to discovering a cure. Once your total accumulated research points exceeds the strength of the plague, the disaster ends.
HELP.LBX          0  4C0AE      19  ?             End Pirate Activity
HELP.LBX          0  4C115     256  en            To end pirate activity in a star system, you need to increase the fleet orbiting that system. Once the fleet strength (determined by number of ships and ship size) is greater than the strength of the pirate's fleet, the pirates cease to destroy freighters.
HELP.LBX          0  4C629      15  en            Destroy a Comet
HELP.LBX          0  4C690     283  en            If one of your colonies is threatened by a comet, you need to increase the number of ships in orbit around that system.  If the total fleet strength (determined by the number and size of the ships) is greater than the  strength of the comet before time is up, the comet is destroyed.
HELP.LBX          0  4CBA4      11                Refit Ships
HELP.LBX          0  4CC0B     449  en            This option is not available in Strategic Combat games. To update the systems or weapons of existing ships in your fleet, select a colony in the system the ship is orbiting. Click the REFIT button on the Colony Production screen.  Select which ship you wish to refit. The ship will be upgraded with any new armor or shields that you have developed. Changes to systems and weapons can then be made on the Ship Design screen (see How to Design Ships).
HELP.LBX          0  4D11F      12                Design Ships
HELP.LBX          0  4D186     677  en            Not available in Strategic Combat games. Click on the DESIGN button on the Colony Production screen and select which size you want to design. The ship will automatically be equipped  with your best drive, armor, computer, and shields. To change a weapon, click on the its name. This calls up a list of all available weapons. Click on the new weapon, choosing any modifications you may want. Click ACCEPT to include that weapon in the design. To delete  a weapon from the design, select NO WEAPON. To add a weapon, run the cursor to the bottom of the current ship weapons list. If there is enough room onboard, you will see an ADD NEW WEAPON option. Add systems in the same way.
HELP.LBX          0  4D69A      13  ?             Get More Help
HELP.LBX          0  4D701     112  en            Right click on most items, buttons, screens throughtout the game to obtain a detailed definition or explanation.
HELP.LBX          0  4DC15      17  ?             Pick New Colonies
HELP.LBX          0  4DC7C     563  en            Each planet has a specific size, climate, gravity, and mineral classification. Choose a planet that best suits your needs: Gaia, Terran, Ocean, Desert, and Tundra climates will allow you to farm. Abundant, Rich, and Ultra Rich mineral classifications will increase your production. Heavy or low gravities will have negative effects on your production if you have no special racial immunities. Remember that building freighters will allow you to transport food to planets with no farming, and enable you to establish colonies  that focus on research or production.
HELP.LBX          0  4E190      16                No Modifications
HELP.LBX          0  4E1F7      27  en            You shouldn't ever see this
HELP.LBX          0  4E70B      11                Heavy Mount
HELP.LBX          0  4E772     110  en            Increases the damage of a weapon by +50% and doubles the range of the weapon  at the cost of double the space.
HELP.LBX          0  4EC86      16                Increased Damage
HELP.LBX          0  4ECED      51  en            Increases the maximum damage of the weapon by +50%.
HELP.LBX          0  4F201      13                Point Defense
HELP.LBX          0  4F268     176  en            Weapons take up half the normal space but range damage penalties are doubled for purposes of energy weapon strength loss. Point defense weapons have a +25% chance to hit bonus.
HELP.LBX          0  4F77C       9                Auto Fire
HELP.LBX          0  4F7E3     146  en            Allows the weapon to be fired three separate times with a -20 chance to hit each time. Auto Fire increases the cost and space of a weapon by +50%.
HELP.LBX          0  4FCF7      14                Armor Piercing
HELP.LBX          0  4FD5E     100  en            Halves the value of enemy armor and adds a +3 chance to breach the armor and inflict internal damage
HELP.LBX          0  50272      15                Shield Piercing
HELP.LBX          0  502D9     115  en            Shield piercing weapons are completely unaffected by any shields except those with the Hard Shields special device.
HELP.LBX          0  507ED      10                Continuous
HELP.LBX          0  50854      49  en            Increases the chance of the weapon to hit by +30.
HELP.LBX          0  50D68      16  es            No Range Penalty
HELP.LBX          0  50DCF      56  en            The strength of the weapon will not be reduced by range.
HELP.LBX          0  512E3      10                Enveloping
HELP.LBX          0  5134A      73  en            Inflicts normal damage to all four shields of the target, simultaneously.
HELP.LBX          0  5185E      15                Heavily Armored
HELP.LBX          0  518C5      51  en            Missiles take 10 hits instead of 4 to be destroyed.
HELP.LBX          0  51DD9       4                Fast
HELP.LBX          0  51E40      53  it            Missiles move +4 squares faster per turn than normal.
HELP.LBX          0  52354       7                Evasive
HELP.LBX          0  523BB      73  en            Allows a missile to dodge enemy attack. Adds +30% to a missile's defense.
HELP.LBX          0  528CF      11                Info Screen
HELP.LBX          0  52936     225  en            The Info Screen allows you to look up information, view current and historical data, check messages, review your technology, change your current research, adjust tax rates, and turn the Resource and Galaxy windows on and off.
HELP.LBX          0  52E4A      23  ?             Info: Subscreen Buttons
HELP.LBX          0  52EB1      57  en            Select the subscreen you wish to view with these buttons.
HELP.LBX          0  533C5      23  ?             Info: Maintenance Chart
HELP.LBX          0  5342C     117  en            This window shows your current income and your maintanence costs as a percentage of income in each of six categories.
HELP.LBX          0  53940      15                Info: Reference
HELP.LBX          0  539A7      86  en            This subscreen allows you to select a category or "how to" topic for more information.
HELP.LBX          0  53EBB      29  ?             Reference: Category Subscreen
HELP.LBX          0  53F22      64  en            Provides information on the topics within the selected category.
HELP.LBX          0  54436      29  en            Reference: "How to" Subscreen
HELP.LBX          0  5449D      52  en            Provides information on the selected "how to" topic.
HELP.LBX          0  549B1      18  ?             Info: Turn Summary
HELP.LBX          0  54A18     263  en            This screen displays a current, scrollable, list of messages requiring your attention. If you click on a colony-related message, you will be transported to the appropriate colony to deal with the situation there, then brought back to this subscreen when finished.
HELP.LBX          0  54F2C      21  ?             Info: Race Statistics
HELP.LBX          0  54F93     221  en            Information about yourself and each of the races you are currently in contact with is displayed on this subscreen. If there are more than four races to be displayed, clicking on the "More" button will show you the others.
HELP.LBX          0  554A7      17  ?             Info: Tech Review
HELP.LBX          0  5550E     177  en            All the technology you have researched or otherwise received is displayed in the scrollable list window. Pointing to an item will display a picture and description of that item.
HELP.LBX          0  55A22      19  ?             Info: History Graph
HELP.LBX          0  55A89     246  en            This screen provides you with a graphical representation of how you and the other races you are in contact with are doing. You can change the information that is integrated into the graphs by clicking on any of the factor buttons below the graph.
HELP.LBX          0  56004      85  en            \x0ARight-click on any application to display a brief description of that appliction.
HELP.LBX          0  5657F     102  en            \x0ALeft-click on the either the field name or any application to select that technology for research.
HELP.LBX          0  56AFA      85  en            \x0AClick on a category button to display a list of other fields under that category.
HELP.LBX          0  5700E      19  ?             Select New Research
HELP.LBX          0  57075     175  en            All the technologies available to you for your next research project are shown under their appropriate categories (Construction, Biology, etc.) along with their research cost.
HELP.LBX          0  57589      23  ?             Change Current Research
HELP.LBX          0  575F0     349  en            All the technologies available to you for research projects are shown under their appropriate categories (Construction, Biology, etc.) along with their research costs adjusted for any prior research. The field you are currently researching is displayed in a different color. \x0ALeft-click on "CANCEL" if you do not wish to change research projects.
HELP.LBX          0  57B04      15                Technology List
HELP.LBX          0  57B6B     304  en            This display shows the fields yet to be researched within a given category. If the current or previous project is within the selected category, it will be shown in a different color. \x0ALeft-click the "CANCEL" button or anywhere outside of the list window to close it and return to the selection window.
HELP.LBX          0  5807F      12                Races Screen
HELP.LBX          0  580E6     285  en            This is your primary diplomacy screen. Here you can check on your relationships, treaties and spies. You can also assign spies to other races, move them from race to race or bring them home. Pick up a spy by left-clicking on a spy icon. Then click again to drop the spy where you wish.
HELP.LBX          0  585FA      26  ?             Races: Individual Displays
HELP.LBX          0  58661     742  en            The multi-color bar in the middle of an individual race display shows you your current relative relationship with the race. To the right of that, you can see your current treaty status. \x0A\x0AThe spies you  currently have assigned to this race are shown as icons and their  current mission is indicated by one of the highlighted buttons at the  bottom of the display. Espionage has the spies attempting to steal  technology.  Sabotage has the spies attempting to destroy buildings.  Hide just has the spies awaiting orders.  You can change the spies' mission  by clicking on a different button. \x0A\x0AFinally, at the bottom right corner of  the screen you see your current supply of unassigned agents along with your  current agent bonus.
HELP.LBX          0  58B75      13                Races: Agents
HELP.LBX          0  58BDC      91  en            Your current supply of unassigned agents is shown here along with your current agent bonus.
HELP.LBX          0  590F0      20  ?             Races: Ignore Button
HELP.LBX          0  59157     192  en            Clicking on this button will allow you to pick a race whose diplomatic overtures you wish to ignore. When the mouse pointer turns to "who?" click on the picture of the race you want to ignore.
HELP.LBX          0  5966B      20  ?             Races: Report Button
HELP.LBX          0  596D2     204  en            Clicking on this button will allow you to select a race for which you wish to see a current report. When the mouse pointer turns to "who?" click on the picture of the race on which you want a report made.
HELP.LBX          0  59BE6      22  ?             Races: Audience Button
HELP.LBX          0  59C4D     190  en            Clicking on this button will allow you to select a race you wish to make diplomatic contact with. When the mouse pointer turns to "who?" click on the picture of the race you want to contact.
HELP.LBX          0  5A161      17                Report: Subscreen
HELP.LBX          0  5A1C8     378  en            This screen shows you the latest information available on the selected race. It includes a picture of the race's leader, a description of their personality, any known spies they have in your empire, a list of their alliances and wars, and a list of their technological achievements. The age of the report should be considered when relying on the report's informational accuracy.
HELP.LBX          0  5A6DC      20  ?             xAudience: Main Menu
HELP.LBX          0  5A743     142  en            Select a category of diplomatic action from the menu of choices. Selections that are presently unavailable are shown in reduced intensity.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  5ACBE     135  en            This selection allows you to discuss make or break a treaty, declare war, or encourage the other race to act against a third party.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  5B239      51  en            This lets you forge or break a trade agreement.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  5B7B4      54  en            Picking this will let you discuss a research swap.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  5BD2F      68  en            "Tribute" is the selection you want if appeasement is your goal.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  5C2AA     102  en            Threatening people is the last resort for some, the first choice for others, but rarely makes friends.
HELP.LBX          0  5C7BE      14                xTreaties Menu
HELP.LBX          0  5C825     150  en            This menu gives you options related to treaties and declarations of war. Selections that are presently unavailable are shown in reduced intensity.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  5DE11      47  en            Select "CANCEL" to return to the previous menu.
HELP.LBX          0  5E325      21  ?             Treaties: Select Race
HELP.LBX          0  5E38C      70  en            Select the race you wish this race to break their treaty with.\x0A\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  5E8A0      16  ?             War: Select Race
HELP.LBX          0  5E907      63  en            Select the race you wish this race to declare war upon.\x0A\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  5EE1B      10                Trade Menu
HELP.LBX          0  5EE82     159  en            From this menu you may choose to make either a cash or technology trade agreement. You may also elect to break a current trade agreement if one exists.\x0A\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  5F396      18  ?             Trade: Cash Amount
HELP.LBX          0  5F3FD      55  en            Select the cash value for your trade agreement.\x0A\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  5F911      17                Trade: Technology
HELP.LBX          0  5F978      79  en            Select the technology level you wish to include in the trade agreement.\x0A\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  5FE8C      29  ?             Technology: Select Technology
HELP.LBX          0  5FEF3     211  en            From the scrollable list of offered technology, select an item to swap for an item of yours. The other race will then decide if they like what you offer and pick something of yours they want in exchange.\x0A\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  60407      12                Tribute Menu
HELP.LBX          0  6046E      65  en            Select the type of tribute you want to give to this race.\x0A\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  60982      20  ?             Tribute: Cash Amount
HELP.LBX          0  609E9      45  en            Select the cash value of your "gift."\x0A\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  60EFD      19                Tribute: Technology
HELP.LBX          0  60F64     123  en            From the scrollable list, select the item of technology you wish to provide to this race as a token of your esteem.\x0A\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  61478       9                Star Date
HELP.LBX          0  614DF     124  en            The star date tells you how long you've been playing the game. Each time  you press next turn, the star date increases by .1
HELP.LBX          0  619F3      11                Game Button
HELP.LBX          0  61A5A     195  en            From this popup, you can change game settings, load a previously-saved game or save the current game. In addition, you can turn game music on or off. Also, sound effects can be toggled on or off.
HELP.LBX          0  61F6E      15                Treasury Window
HELP.LBX          0  61FD5     159  en            From this window you see the current number of credits (BC for billion credits) at your disposal. You may left-click in this window to change your tax rate\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  624EA      13                Income Window
HELP.LBX          0  62550     163  en            This window displays your current income or, more precisely, the  number of credits (BC) you receive each turn. If this number is negative,  it will appear in red.
HELP.LBX          0  62A64      21  ?             Command Points Window
HELP.LBX          0  62ACB     720  en            Command points affect the maintenance you pay for ships in your fleet.  Each ship you build removes points from your reserve, while each station  you build adds points to the reserve. Warlords gain 2 per colony, while  Imperium goverments increases your reserve by 50% You may left-click in this window to get a summary of your command points.\x0A\x0A The first number in this window shows your current command point reserve.  If this number is positive, you can safely build more ships. \x0A\x0A If the number is negative, each point is costing you 10 BC per turn.  The second number, displayed in parentheses, shows your total command points. \x0A\x0A The following chart breaks down how command points are calculated.
HELP.LBX          0  6355A      11                Food Window
HELP.LBX          0  635C1      92  en            This window displays how much NET food is being produced each turn,  throughout your empire.
HELP.LBX          0  63AD5      17                Freighters Window
HELP.LBX          0  63B3C     272  en            This window displays two pieces of data relating to freighters. The first value is the amount of available freighters, or those NOT in use. The total number of freighters appears second and in parentheses.  You may "sell back" freighters by "left-clicking" in this window.
HELP.LBX          0  64050      15                Research Window
HELP.LBX          0  640B7     534  en            This windows shows the status of your current research efforts. During most of the research, your progress is shown in turns. This is an approximate value. When your accumulated research points reach the stated  cost of the item you are researching, you will be given a percent chance  to achieve the breakthrough each turn thereafter.\x0A\x0A The second line in this window shows  the current number of research points (RPs) your empire generates each turn. You may left-click in this window to change your current field of research.
HELP.LBX          0  645CB      15                Colony Overview
HELP.LBX          0  64632     293  en            Pressing the "Colonies" button takes you to the Colony Overview screen.  You will see all of your colonies, what they are currently producing and  the amount of population assigned to farming, production and research.  You can alter these values here or jump directly to the Colony screen.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  64B46      15                Planet Overview
HELP.LBX          0  64BAD     360  en            Pressing the "Planets" button takes you to the Planet Overview screen. Here you will see all of the planets you have discovered. Using filters,  you can reduce the list to show planets that are not enemy-controlled,  planets that produce food, planets where production is not hindered, etc.\x0A\x0A Once filtered, you can deploy ships to colonize a planet.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  650C1      14                Fleet Overview
HELP.LBX          0  65128     288  en            Pressing the "Fleet" button takes you to the Fleet Overview screen where you can manage all the ships in your empire. Scrapping ships, relocating ships to another system, and assigning or removing officers can be done  here. You may also give movement orders to any ship from this screen.
HELP.LBX          0  6563C      16  ?             Next Turn Button
HELP.LBX          0  656A3     382  en            Press the "Turn" button when you are done entering orders for the current  turn. If you are in a "hot-seat" game, play continues with the next player.  If you are in a "network" game, play continues when all players have  entered their orders. Otherwise, non-player opponents will plot their moves  and the computer will display the results in the "reports" phase of the  next turn.
HELP.LBX          0  65BB7      15                Leader Overview
HELP.LBX          0  65C1E     440  en            Pressing the "Leaders" button takes you to the Leader Screen. Here you can assign or dismiss current leaders, hire leaders currently in the "for hire" queue, or deactivate assigned leaders to a "waiting" pool.  This screen shows information on all available leaders, so you can see how  much maintenance a leader costs or will cost, and any skills that he or she  brings to your empire. Detailed help on leader skills is available here.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  66132      13                Race Overview
HELP.LBX          0  66199     241  en            Pressing the "Races" button takes you to the Race Screen. Here you  will get an overview of your contacts with other races in the game. You  can set and/or nullify peace treaties and assign spies to any one of several nefarious missions.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  666AD      13                Info Overview
HELP.LBX          0  66714     262  en            Press the "Info" button to take you to the Info Screen. Here you will get detailed help on every aspect of the game, from technology advances to  effects of different governments. Bars and charts show your empire's  development relative to all of your opponents.
HELP.LBX          0  66C28      14  en            Zoom In Button
HELP.LBX          0  66C8F     385  en            Pressing the "+" button zooms IN from your current map, allowing you a closer look at the galaxy. A "zoom box" will appear. Move the box with  your mouse to the area you want to see in more detail. When you press the left mouse, the map will zoom in. Alternatively, you may continue pressing the "-" button. The zoom box will get smaller as you are, in effect,  zooming in further.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  671A3      15  ?             Zoom Out Button
HELP.LBX          0  6720A     131  en            Pressing the "-" button zooms OUT from your current map, condensing the number of stars and allowing you to see MORE of the galaxy.
HELP.LBX          0  6771E      16                Diplomacy Lights
HELP.LBX          0  67785     207  en            This is where you will be notified if a player seeks to negotiate  with you. If you see one of the circles lit, go to the RACES screen to initiate diplomatic interactions. Only available in multiplayer games
HELP.LBX          0  67C99      24  ?             Multi-Player Done Lights
HELP.LBX          0  67D00     176  en            This is where you will be notified when a player has completed his turn. As each player completes his turn in a multi-player game, a circle will be filled with his player-color
HELP.LBX          0  68214      26  ?             Close Fleet Operations Box
HELP.LBX          0  6827B     226  en            Closes the fleet operations box. Clicking on any fleet opens the box. You can re-open it and cycle to your "next" fleet, by pressing F2. Pressing F1 goes back one fleet. If you have no fleets, an enemy fleet may be substituted
HELP.LBX          0  6878F      15                Attack Anatares
HELP.LBX          0  687F6     187  en            If you have a Dimensional Portal, you may, at any time, send a fleet through the portal to attack the mighty Antaran empire. All ships selected will be sent at the start of the next turn.
HELP.LBX          0  68D0A      15                Colonize Planet
HELP.LBX          0  68D71     226  en            If you have a colony ship in the current fleet, you may use it to colonize any planet in the system you are orbiting. A system display will replace the fleet operations box. From this box, you will select a planet to colonize.
HELP.LBX          0  69285      19  ?             Engage Enemy Forces
HELP.LBX          0  692EC     184  en            You may engage enemy forces in the system you are orbiting by selecting this button. All selected ships will be sent into battle. The attack will be launched during the following turn.
HELP.LBX          0  69800      17                Unload Transports
HELP.LBX          0  69867     165  en            Selecting this button will unload your marines to reinforce a planet. You will be shown a special screen where you will be given limited control over the  bombarment
HELP.LBX          0  69D7B      13                Build Outpost
HELP.LBX          0  69DE2     317  en            If you have an outpost ship in the fleet and are orbiting a system  containing at least one planet, you can place an outpost by selecting  this button. Building the outpost comsumes the ship. Outposts are helpful when you want to extend your range but don't want to force colonisists to live on a worthless rock-world
HELP.LBX          0  6A2F6      16                Fleet Operations
HELP.LBX          0  6A35D     386  en            From this box, ships will be given orders. To select or de-select a ship,  left-click on its picture. You can select or de-select more than one ship  by holding down the left mouse button and moving the mouse across all  ships you wish to select. Pressing the ALL button will toggle all ships  on and off. Detailed ship information can be obtained by right-clicking on the ship picture.
HELP.LBX          0  6A8D8     434  en            After you have selected one or more ships, you can send them to a star by  left-clicking on a destination star on the map. As you run your mouse over  a star, a line will be drawn from the fleet icon to the star. Green lines denote valid moves, red denotes invalid ones. A move may be invalid if the  destination is out of range, blocked by a black hole, etc. In the fleet operations box, look at the status line for more information.
HELP.LBX          0  6AE53     315  en            Once you click on a destination star, all selected ships will be  separated into another fleet as they depart the star. If multiple fleets  are leaving a star for separate destinations, they will overlap on the  main map. You may have to click on a fleet icon more than once to see all  fleets at a single location.
HELP.LBX          0  6B367      21  ?             Colony Leaders Button
HELP.LBX          0  6B3CE     100  en            Sends you to the Colony Leaders screen, where you can manage all the  colony leaders in your empire.
HELP.LBX          0  6B8E2      20  ?             Ship Officers Button
HELP.LBX          0  6B949      98  en            Sends you to the Ship Officers screen, where you can manage all the  ship officers in your empire.
HELP.LBX          0  6BE5D      26  ?             Colony Leaders Star System
HELP.LBX          0  6BEC4      98  en            Shows the current star system. You can scan planets and fleets to get a brief description of each.
HELP.LBX          0  6C3D8      26  ?             Colony Leader Descriptions
HELP.LBX          0  6C43F     798  en            This area lists all the colony leaders at your disposal. Each window shows one leader, his or her picture, and pertinent skills. You may press the RIGHT mouse button on each skill to get a brief description of each. If you press the RIGHT mouse button on the leader's picture, the star  system display will flip to the star where he or she is stationed. \x0A\x0A If the leader has not been hired yet, you may attempt to hire him or her by pressing the LEFT mouse button while over the picture. \x0A\x0A Once hired, you may assign the officer to a star system. When you select a leader (left-click on his or her picture), you are assigning him or her  to the star being displayed in the star system window. To change the star system, you must deselect the officer and select a different star system.
HELP.LBX          0  6C954      19  ?             Colony Leader Desc2
HELP.LBX          0  6C9BA     220  en            Note that it takes an officer 5 turns to travel from star system to star system, or from the Pool to any star system. The Officer Pool exists on your home star, so travel from the Pool to your home star is instantaneous.
HELP.LBX          0  6CECE      31  ?             Colony Leaders Star Description
HELP.LBX          0  6CF35     182  en            This is where information will appear as you scan over fleets or planets in the star system display. If a star system has a leader assigned, his or her name will apear in parentheses
HELP.LBX          0  6D449      29  ?             Previous Officers Star System
HELP.LBX          0  6D4B0     120  en            When you click this button, the star system display will "go back" one star in the list of all stars you have colonized.
HELP.LBX          0  6D9C4      25  ?             Next Officers Star System
HELP.LBX          0  6DA2B     125  en            When you click this button, the star system display will advance to the next star in the list of all stars you have colonized
HELP.LBX          0  6DF3F      25  ?             Officer Screen Galaxy Map
HELP.LBX          0  6DFA6     400  en            This is a scaled-down version of the entire galaxy. Stars are shown in the color of its owner, or in a neutral color if it is unowned or undiscovered. If a ship is within contact range, it will be shown here. As you scan  fleets and stars, a brief description is shown in the box below. If you select a star in this window, you will see the planets and their orbits in the  Star System display above.
HELP.LBX          0  6E4BA      37  ?             Officer Screen Galaxy Map Description
HELP.LBX          0  6E521      85  en            As your mouse scans over fleets, information on scanned stars and ships appears here.
HELP.LBX          0  6EA35      26  ?             Officer Screen Hire Button
HELP.LBX          0  6EA9C     742  en            Officers that are initially REJECTED will be placed in a "Hiring Queue". They will stay in this queue for 30 turns, after which they will leave to search out better jobs. They may or may not return again. To place them into your service, you must actually "hire" them.\x0A\x0A Pressing the HIRE button places you in HIRE mode. While in this mode, you can scan over leader pictures and retrieve cost and maintenance  information about a particular leader. If you wish to hire a leader, select his or her picture. You must have enough BC's to cover the initial cost. Maintenance is subtracted each turn from your treasury. Hired officers are placed in your Officer Pool for later assignment.\x0A\x0A To exit HIRE mode, select the CANCEL button.
HELP.LBX          0  6EFB0      26  ?             Officer Screen Pool Button
HELP.LBX          0  6F017     136  en            Moves the officer from his/her current position into the Officer Pool. It does not take any time to move from a star system to the Pool.
HELP.LBX          0  6F52B      29  ?             Officer Screen Dismiss Button
HELP.LBX          0  6F592     125  en            Officers may be dismissed at any time. Once dismissed, an officer is not gone for good, he/she may come back at a later time.
HELP.LBX          0  6FAA6      19  ?             Leave Leader Screen
HELP.LBX          0  6FB0D      55  en            Pressing the RETURN button will exit the Leader screen.
HELP.LBX          0  70021      25  ?             Ship Officers Star System
HELP.LBX          0  70088      98  en            Shows the current star system. You can scan planets and fleets to get a breif description of each.
HELP.LBX          0  7059C      25  ?             Ship Officer Descriptions
HELP.LBX          0  70603     990  en            This area lists all the leaders at your disposal. Each window shows a leader, his/her picture, and pertinent skills. You may press the RIGHT mouse button on each skill to get a brief description of each. If you press the RIGHT mouse button on the leader's picture, the fleet  display will flip to the fleet where he/she is stationed. \x0A\x0A If the leader has not been hired yet, you may attempt to hire him/her by press the LEFT mouse button while over the picture. \x0A\x0A Once hired, you may assign the officer to a ship. After selecting a leader (left-click on his/her picture), a bright border will appear. Then, select any ship in your empire. If the ship is located in the same system as your home star, the assignment is instantaneous. Otherwise, it  will take 5 turns for the leader to travel to the ship. To select a ship from a fleet other than the one shown, either click on the ship in the galaxy map window, or use the left and right arrows to cycle through all your fleets.
HELP.LBX          0  70B17      30  ?             Ship Officers Ship Description
HELP.LBX          0  70B7E     154  en            This is where information will appear as you scan over ships in the current fleet. If a leader has been assigned, his/her name will apear in  parentheses.
HELP.LBX          0  71092      30  ?             Previous Officers Fleet Button
HELP.LBX          0  710F9     107  en            When you click this button, the display will "go back" one fleet in  the list of all fleets in your empire.
HELP.LBX          0  7160D      26  ?             Next Officers Fleet Button
HELP.LBX          0  71674     117  en            When you click this button, the fleet display will advance to the next fleet in the list of all fleet in your empire.
HELP.LBX          0  71B88      30  ?             Ship Officer Screen Galaxy Map
HELP.LBX          0  71BEF     400  en            This is a scaled-down version of the entire galaxy. Stars are shown in the color of its owner, or in a neutral color if it is unowned or undiscovered. If a ship is within contact range, it will be shown here. As you scan  fleets and stars, a breif description is shown in the box below. If you select a fleet in this window, you will see each ship in that fleet displayed in  the fleet display above.
HELP.LBX          0  72103      24  ?             Ship Officers Fleet Grid
HELP.LBX          0  7216A     259  en            Each ship in a fleet is displayed here. As you scan each ship, its name and leader will be seen in the box below. If you wish to assign a leader, you  may select a ship, then select any leader. You may "right-click" on a ship to get more detailed information.
HELP.LBX          0  7267E      23  ?             Ship Officers Up Button
HELP.LBX          0  726E5      48  en            Use the up arrow the scroll up one row of ships.
HELP.LBX          0  72BF9      24  ?             Ship Officers Scroll Bar
HELP.LBX          0  72C60      92  en            Use the scroll bar to scroll quickly up and down the list of all ships in the current fleet.
HELP.LBX          0  73174      25  ?             Ship Officers Down Button
HELP.LBX          0  731DB      52  en            Use the down arrow the scroll down one row of ships.
HELP.LBX          0  736EF      14                Planet Summary
HELP.LBX          0  73756     411  en            Here you will see a list of all known planets. The list can be  sorted by climate, size, or mineral abundance. If a SEND button is selected, the mouse pointer will either be a red circle with a line through it or an arrow pointing to a planet. The red circle indicates that you cannot  send a ship to this system. Once a SEND button has been selected, click on  any valid planet to deploy a ship to that system.
HELP.LBX          0  73C6A       6                Planet
HELP.LBX          0  73CD1     128  en            This column shows the planet in graphic representation, its name (in player colors) and any planet specials or guardian monsters
HELP.LBX          0  741E5       7                Climate
HELP.LBX          0  7424C      72  en            This column shows the planet's CLIMATE and its effect on food production
HELP.LBX          0  74760       7                Gravity
HELP.LBX          0  747C7      76  en            This column shows the planet's GRAVITY and its effect on worker productivity
HELP.LBX          0  74CDB       8                Minerals
HELP.LBX          0  74D42     103  en            This column shows the planet's MINERAL abundance and how it affects  the amount each worker can produce
HELP.LBX          0  75256       4                Size
HELP.LBX          0  752BD      72  en            This column shows the planet's SIZE and its effect on maximum population
HELP.LBX          0  757D1      10                Galaxy Map
HELP.LBX          0  75838     336  en            Within this window, you will see a representation of the entire galaxy. Each colony  ship in your fleet is represented as a "C". Each outpost ship is  represented as an "O". Destination lines show the current destination of  each ship. You may left-click on a star in the galaxy map to move the list  to the first planet in that system.
HELP.LBX          0  75D4D      20  ?             Star description box
HELP.LBX          0  75DB3     412  en            As you move the mouse pointer over each star in the galaxy map, its name  will appear in the box below. Likewise, if you move the mouse over a planet in the list to the left, the name of the system will appear in the box. If  the "SEND COLONY SHIP" or "SEND OUTPOST SHIP" button is selected,  a destination line will be drawn from the closest colony or outpost ship, and travel time, in turns, will be displayed.
HELP.LBX          0  762C7       9                Scroll Up
HELP.LBX          0  7632E      64  en            The scroll up button can be used to scroll up one line at a time
HELP.LBX          0  76842      10                Scroll Bar
HELP.LBX          0  768A9      49  en            Use the scroll bar to scroll one screen at a time
HELP.LBX          0  76DBD      11                Scroll Down
HELP.LBX          0  76E24      68  en            The scroll down button can be used to scroll down one line at a time
HELP.LBX          0  77338      15  ?             Sort By Climate
HELP.LBX          0  7739F     149  en            When "Climate" sort is chosen, the list of known planets will be  sorted by food production, which is the effect different climates have on a planet.
HELP.LBX          0  778B3      16  ?             Sort By Minerals
HELP.LBX          0  7791A     154  en            When "Mineral" sort is chosen, the list of known planets will be  sorted by worker productivity, which is the effect mineral abundance has on each planet.
HELP.LBX          0  77E2E      12  ?             Sort By Size
HELP.LBX          0  77E95     136  en            When "Size" sort is chosen, the list of known planets will be sorted by maximum population, which is the effect size has on each planet.
HELP.LBX          0  783A9      21  ?             Enemy Presence Filter
HELP.LBX          0  78410     198  en            When this button is active, the list of known planets will be stripped of all planets that have an enemy presence in the system. An "enemy presence" is any enemy ship or monster orbiting the system.
HELP.LBX          0  78924      21  ?             Normal Gravity Filter
HELP.LBX          0  7898B     143  en            When this button is active, the list of known planets will be stripped  of all planets that would receive a negative worker productivity bonus.
HELP.LBX          0  78E9F      26  ?             Hostile Environment Filter
HELP.LBX          0  78F06     163  en            When this button is active, the list of known planets will be stripped  of all planets with a hostile climate. Hostile climates are those that do not produce food.
HELP.LBX          0  7941A      23  ?             Mineral Abundant Filter
HELP.LBX          0  79481     193  en            When this button is active, the list of known planets will be stripped  of all planets that have a low mineral abundance. These are planets that  do not have at least one production per worker.
HELP.LBX          0  79995      23  en            Planets In Range Filter
HELP.LBX          0  799FC     279  en            When this button is active, the list of known planets will include planets that are in range of one of your colonies. You might want to turn this filter off to see which planets are nearby. As your fuel cell technology increases, or you expand out, more planets will be in range.
HELP.LBX          0  79F10      17  ?             Send Colony Ships
HELP.LBX          0  79F77     140  en            To send a colony ship to a system, you must activate this button. If the button  will not activate, then you have no colony ships to deploy.
HELP.LBX          0  7A48B      18  ?             Send Outpost Ships
HELP.LBX          0  7A4F2     143  en            To send an outpost ship to a system, you must activate this button. If the button  will not activate, then you have no outpost ships to deploy.
HELP.LBX          0  7AA06      19  ?             Leave Planet Screen
HELP.LBX          0  7AA6D      96  en            Pressing the RETURN button will exit the Planets screen and return you  to the main game screen.
HELP.LBX          0  7AF81      23  ?             Fleet Screen Galaxy Map
HELP.LBX          0  7AFE8     867  en            The entire galaxy is displayed here. Each planet is represented in the  color of its owner. If a planet is unowned or undiscovered, it will appear in a neutral color. As the mouse pointer scans over each planet, its name will appear in the galaxy map description box below. If a leader has been assigned to the star, his/her name will appear in parenthesis.\x0A\x0A  When the "Relocate" button has been selected, you will select source and destination stars from this window. \x0A\x0A  As you select individual ships from the grid to the right, you can assign  destinations by clicking on a star from this window. \x0A\x0A A fleet will only appear in the galaxy map if it is within contact range. As your mouse pointer scans over each fleet, its owner will appear in the box below. As you select fleets from this window, they will be displayed in detail to the right.
HELP.LBX          0  7B4FC      22  ?             Fleet Screen Ship Grid
HELP.LBX          0  7B563     750  en            From this window, each fleet will be displayed in detail. As you enter the screen, if you had a fleet selected in the "Fleet Movement" box on  the MAIN screen, it will be displayed here. Otherwise the first fleet in your empire will be displayed. \x0A\x0A By scanning each ship, you can get a short description in the ship  description to the lower left of this screen. By pressing the RIGHT mouse button while over any of your ships, you will get a more-detailed  description. After selecting ships from this grid, you may then give them "move" orders to any star within range by selecting a star from the  galaxy map window. If ships are selected as you scan stars, a green line indicates a valid destination. Red lines denote invalid destinations.
HELP.LBX          0  7BA77      22  ?             Fleet Screen Scroll Up
HELP.LBX          0  7BADE     146  en            Only sixteen ships may displayed at one time. If the fleet has in excess of sixteen ships, you may scroll up row of ships by selecting this button
HELP.LBX          0  7BFF2      23  ?             Fleet Screen Scroll Bar
HELP.LBX          0  7C059     102  en            Moving the scroll bar up and down is a quick way to adjust the current range of ships being displayed.
HELP.LBX          0  7C56D      31  ?             Fleet Screen Galaxy Description
HELP.LBX          0  7C5D4      84  en            This window displays infomation as you scan ships and stars in the galaxy map window
HELP.LBX          0  7CAE8      34  ?             Fleet Screen Previous Fleet Button
HELP.LBX          0  7CB4F     281  en            Pressing this button will "go back" one fleet in the list of all fleets in your empire. Note that as the filter buttons are selected,  a fleet may be skipped. For example, if you are filtering out combat ships,  then a fleet must contain at least one non-combat ship to be selected
HELP.LBX          0  7D063      30  ?             Fleet Screen Next Fleet Button
HELP.LBX          0  7D0CA     257  en            Pressing this button will display the next fleet in your empire. Note  that as the filter buttons are selected, a fleet may be skipped. For example, if you are filtering out non-combat ships, then fleets containing at least one combat ship will be selected.
HELP.LBX          0  7D5DE      28  ?             Fleet Screen Ship Descrption
HELP.LBX          0  7D645     293  en            As you scan ships in the grid window to the right, a brief description of the ship will appear here. If a ship officer is on board, his/her picture will be displayed as well. For a more detailed description, press the  RIGHT mouse button when the pointer is over the ship (in the grid window).
HELP.LBX          0  7DB59      24  ?             Fleet Screen Scroll Down
HELP.LBX          0  7DBC0     104  en            If the fleet has in excess of sixteen ships, you may scroll down row  of ships by selecting this button.
HELP.LBX          0  7E0D4      23  ?             Fleet Screen All Button
HELP.LBX          0  7E13B      58  en            Pressing the ALL button will select all ships in the fleet
HELP.LBX          0  7E64F      28  ?             Fleet Screen Relocate Button
HELP.LBX          0  7E6B6     807  en            Pressing the RELOCATE button allows you to send ships built at one star to be given orders to move to another star. As soon as the ship construction is complete, the ship will be given orders to move to a destination star. The travel time does not change. Be warned that the ships will be sent irrespective of the conditions at the destination  star. Which, is to say, that if there are enemy ships or enemy star bases there, combat will ensue.\x0A\x0A You may cancel relocation orders at star by selecting the the same  source and destination stars. You may cancel all relocation orders by pressing ALT-F5.\x0A\x0A You may direct all ships built to be sent to the same star by pressing F4 and then selecting destination star.\x0A\x0A Pressing the RELOCATE button again will take you out of relocation mode.
HELP.LBX          0  7EBCA      25  ?             Fleet Screen Scrap Button
HELP.LBX          0  7EC31     349  en            This button allows you to scrap one or more ships. First, select the ships you want the scrap and press the SCRAP button. Your treasury will increase by the scrap value of each ship. In addition, as you dismantle captured enemy ships, there is a chance you will be able to learn new technology. This is the ONLY way you can learn ANTARAN technology!
HELP.LBX          0  7F145      28  ?             Fleet Screen Officers Button
HELP.LBX          0  7F1AC     152  en            This button takes you to the Officer Screen, where you can manage all the officers in your empire. This button will be inactive if you have no officers.
HELP.LBX          0  7F6C0      27  ?             Fleet Screen Support Button
HELP.LBX          0  7F727     287  en            The support button allows you to determine whether support (non-combat) ships appear in the ship grid window above. If the button is lit,  support ships will be shown. Additionally, if this button is NOT lit, fleets with only support ships will be skipped as you cycle through all fleets
HELP.LBX          0  7FC3B      26  ?             Fleet Screen Combat Button
HELP.LBX          0  7FCA2     273  en            The support button allows you to determine whether combat ships appear  in the ship grid window above. If the button is lit, combat ships will  be shown. Additionally, if this button is NOT lit, fleets with only combat ships will be skipped as you cycle through all fleets.
HELP.LBX          0  801B6      18  ?             Leave Fleet Screen
HELP.LBX          0  8021D      94  en            Pressing the RETURN button will exit the Fleet screen and return you  to the main game screen.
HELP.LBX          0  80731      18  ?             Designed Ship Name
HELP.LBX          0  80798      78  en            Click here to change the name of your ship, up to a maximum of 14  characters.
HELP.LBX          0  80CAC      16  en            Drives and Armor
HELP.LBX          0  80D13     732  en            The left panel shows the current drive and armor type. Hyperspace drives have two pertinent pieces of data -- distance (parsecs/turn) and combat speed.  Distance is used outside of combat and determines the maximum distance your ship can travel in one turn. Fuel Cell technology also affects distance.  Combat speed determines how far your ship can travel in one combat round.\x0A\x0A Armor is non-ablative and provides basic protection in two ways. It can  reinforce the hull, allowing it to take more structural points before the ship is destroyed. It will provide sturdy outer shell, which must be pierced before internal damage can be done. \x0A\x0A Each ship will be fitted with the best armor and hyperspace drives  available.
HELP.LBX          0  81227      21  en            Shields and Computers
HELP.LBX          0  8128E     984  en            The right panel shows information on shields, computers, and ship combat modifiers. Shields protect the ship from incoming missile, torpedo, and beam fire. The strength of the shield is ablative. As each shield takes damage, its strength is reduced. When the strength reaches 0, armor points are reduced. The class rating of a shield is important in that this is the amount of damage taken off EACH attack as long as the shield generator is working. This amount comes off BEFORE any damage  is done to shield strength. So, even if the strength of a shield is 0,  as long as the shield generator is intact, a class 5 shield takes off 5 points of damage. \x0A\x0A Each ship equipped with shields has 4 shields spread in 90-degree arcs. \x0A\x0A Computers make it easy to hit with all beam weapons. \x0A\x0A Missile evasion refers to the ship's ability to dodge incoming missiles. Each point reduces the chance to hit by 1. So that 50% evasion reduces each missile's chance to hit by 50.
HELP.LBX          0  817A2      10                Hull Sizes
HELP.LBX          0  819BC     225  en            X275.150 \x0A\x0A           * Ships larger than destroyers can only be built on planets with a star base, battle station,  or star fortress. In addition, certain technology is required to build Titan and Doom Star class ships
HELP.LBX          0  81D1D      19  ?             Design Ship Picture
HELP.LBX          0  81D84      66  en            This window shows which icon will represent your ship in the game.
HELP.LBX          0  82298      21  ?             Previous Ship Picture
HELP.LBX          0  822FF      66  en            You can "go back" one picture in the list by pressing this button.
HELP.LBX          0  82813      17  ?             Next Ship Picture
HELP.LBX          0  8287A      71  en            You can show the next ship picture in the list by pressing this button.
HELP.LBX          0  82D8E      21  ?             Maximum Space Allowed
HELP.LBX          0  82DF5     141  en            This window shows the maximum space allowed for the current class of ships. To change the class, select a size from the buttons to the right.
HELP.LBX          0  83309      14                Ships' Weapons
HELP.LBX          0  83370     452  en            This area shows the weapons currently loaded onto your ship. Just to the  left of each weapon name, + and - buttons allow you to change the number of weapons mounted in each slot. To the right, you will see a brief overview of each weapon, including damage, arcs of fire, cost, space, and any special effects. Bear in mind this data refers to ONE weapon, so that if you have 10 weapons mounted, each taking up 5 space, the whole slot takes up 50 space.
HELP.LBX          0  838EB     593  en            To add extra weapons, click in the open area just below the last weapon  displayed, if any. The words "Add new weapon" will appear. If these words do not appear, then you are unable to add any more weapons, due to space restrictions. You may only have 8 different types of weapons on each ship. \x0A\x0A To replace a weapon, click on its slot. The weapon text will highlight just before you click. Whether you click on an open slot or an occupied slot, you will then see a list of available weapons. \x0A\x0A If you to clear a weapon slot, select "NO WEAPON" on the list of  available weapons.
HELP.LBX          0  83DFF      15                Special Systems
HELP.LBX          0  83E66     373  en            This window will show any special systems currently on your ship. By clicking on an open slot, watch for the words "Add New Special System" to appear before clicking. Like weapons, if you select an occupied slot, you will be replacing the system with a new one. When replacing a system,  if you select "No System" on the list of available systems, the slot will be cleared.
HELP.LBX          0  843E1      64  en            Click the CANCEL button to exit without adding a special system.
HELP.LBX          0  848F5      12                Clear Design
HELP.LBX          0  8495C     134  en            Clicking the Clear button cancels all modifications you have made to  the current design and starts with a new, empty design template.
HELP.LBX          0  84E70      13                Cancel Design
HELP.LBX          0  84ED7     153  en            To cancel the current design and undo all changes, click the Cancel button. After clicking the cancel button, you will return to the Colony Build screen.
HELP.LBX          0  853EB      12                Build Design
HELP.LBX          0  85452     386  en            When you click the Build button, your current design will be saved.\x0A\x0A You will be taken to the Colony Build screen, where you must then add the  designed ship to the list of buildings and ships to be built. \x0A\x0A If you try to put too much equipment on a ship, space available falls below 0, and you will be unable to complete the design. The Build button will be unselectable.
HELP.LBX          0  85966       9                Ship Cost
HELP.LBX          0  859CD      38  en            Cost of the ship in production points.
HELP.LBX          0  85EE1      15                Space Available
HELP.LBX          0  85F48     260  en            Amount of space left in the current design. This value is updated and made  available in the background as you replace weapons and special systems. If this number is below 0, you will not be able to complete the design, and the BUILD button will appear dimmed.
HELP.LBX          0  8645C      23  en            Beam Weapons In Display
HELP.LBX          0  864C3      97  en            When this button is selected, all BEAM weapons are removed from the list of  weapon replacements.
HELP.LBX          0  869D7      26  en            Missile Weapons In Display
HELP.LBX          0  86A3E     100  en            When this button is selected, all MISSILE weapons are removed from the list of  weapon replacements.
HELP.LBX          0  86F52      23  en            Bomb Weapons In Display
HELP.LBX          0  86FB9      97  en            When this button is selected, all BOMB weapons are removed from the list of  weapon replacements.
HELP.LBX          0  874CD      33  en            Special Device Weapons In Display
HELP.LBX          0  87534     107  en            When this button is selected, all SPECIAL DEVICE weapons are removed from  the list of weapon replacements.
HELP.LBX          0  87A48      25  ?             Cancel Weapon Replacement
HELP.LBX          0  87AAF     159  en            Selecting this button will cancel the current weapon choice and return to the main design screen. You may also cancel by clicking outside the  replacement box.
HELP.LBX          0  87FC3      25  ?             Accept Weapon Replacement
HELP.LBX          0  8802A     206  en            Selecting this button, or clicking on a selecting weapon, will accept the  current weapon choice and return to the main design screen. If you select NO WEAPON the current weapon design slot will be cleared.
HELP.LBX          0  8853E      11                Weapon Arcs
HELP.LBX          0  885A5     277  en            Weapon arcs are changed by selecting arcs from this menu. Arcs are in 120 degrees extending from the FORWARD, FORWARD-EXTENDED, BACK, AND BACK-EXTENDED areas of the ship. You may have only one arc per weapon. Note that missiles and torpedoes have 360 degree (FULL) weapon arcs.
HELP.LBX          0  88AB9      12                Weapon Racks
HELP.LBX          0  88B20     225  en            Missiles and torpedoes have racks. Each rack stores one missile volley. As you fire missiles, one volley of missiles get expended. When you are out of volleys, you may not fire that missile weapon again until the next combat.
HELP.LBX          0  89034      20                Weapon Modifications
HELP.LBX          0  8909B     241  en            Weapons may be modified to enhance their effectiveness. You must first have  researched the modifications for the particular weapon, and not all weapons  allow all modifications. The abbreviation for each modification appears in parentheses.
HELP.LBX          0  895AF      16  ?             Heavy Mount (HV)
HELP.LBX          0  89616     409  en            Heavy Mount (HV) weapons are larger platform versions of the normal weapon,  inflicting one and a half times the normal amount of damage, halving the actual range for purposes of dissipation and to hit penalties, and requiring double the base amount of space and cost. Heavy mount weapons can not fire at missiles or fighters due to their slow targeting.  Heavy mount and point defense are mutually exclusive.
HELP.LBX          0  89B2A      18  ?             Point Defense (PD)
HELP.LBX          0  89B91     535  en            Point Defense weapons take up only half the normal amount of space normally  required and cost half the normal amount, but inflict only half damage. Furthermore, the  effective range is doubled for purposes of computing the energy dissipation and to hit  penalties, but point defense weapons have a +25% bonus to hit.  Finally, point defense  weapons will always fire just before a missile hits a ship or fighters engage the ship if  the point defense weapons have not yet fired.  Heavy Mount and Point Defense are  mutually exclusive.
HELP.LBX          0  8A0A5      19  ?             Armor Piercing (AP)
HELP.LBX          0  8A10C     256  en            Armor piercing weapons automatically penetrate any type of armor except  xentronium, damaging the ships structure and internals directly.  Armor piercing increases the size and cost of a weapon system by +50% and requires 1 level of  refinement to be used.
HELP.LBX          0  8A620      15                Continuous (CO)
HELP.LBX          0  8A687     223  en            Continuous allows a beam weapon to fire over a longer duration, increasing the  weapons chance to hit by +25. Continuous increases the size and cost of a weapon  system by +50% and requires 1 level of refinement to be used.
HELP.LBX          0  8AB9B      25  en            Not Reduced By Range (NR)
HELP.LBX          0  8AC02     283  en            Not Reduced By Range applies to energy weapons and torpedoes that diminish in strength by  range. By focusing the beam and eliminating the decrease in damage. No range  dissipation increases the size and cost of a weapon system by +25%, and requires 1  level of refinement to employ.
HELP.LBX          0  8B116      20  ?             Shield Piercing (SP)
HELP.LBX          0  8B17D     201  en            Shield Piercing allows the weapon to ignore all aspects of shield. Shield piercing  requires +50% more space and cost, and cannot be used until 1 levels of refinement  have been achieved with a weapon.
HELP.LBX          0  8B691      13                Autofire (AF)
HELP.LBX          0  8B6F8     217  en            Autofire allows the weapon to fire 3 separate times in rapid succession,  each with a -20% chance to hit. Autofire increase the size and cost of a weapon  system by +50% and requires 2 levels of refinement to be used.
HELP.LBX          0  8BC0C      16                Enveloping (ENV)
HELP.LBX          0  8BC73     214  en            Enveloping surrounds the target with the blast and strikes to all four sides of  the ship, simultaneously. Enveloping increases the size and cost of a weapon by  +100% and requires 2 levels of refinement to employ.
HELP.LBX          0  8C187       9                Mirv (MV)
HELP.LBX          0  8C1EE     211  en            Mirv missiles carry 4 separate warheads, which separate from the missile just  before impact. Mirv missiles increase the size and cost of a weapon system by +100%  and requires 2 levels of refinement to be used.
HELP.LBX          0  8C702      11                ECCM (ECCM)
HELP.LBX          0  8C769     240  en            ECCM missiles equipped with electronic counter measures, halve the chance of  a missile being jammed by enemy electronic counter measures. ECCM increases the size  and cost of a missile by +25% and requires 1 level of refinement to be used.
HELP.LBX          0  8CC7D      22  ?             Armored Missiles (ARM)
HELP.LBX          0  8CCE4     170  en            Armored missiles are take twice the amount of damage to destroy. Armored  increase the cost and space of a missile by +25%  and require 1 level of  refinement to be used.
HELP.LBX          0  8D1F8      19  ?             Fast Missiles (FST)
HELP.LBX          0  8D25F     238  en            Fast Missiles increase the speed of a missile in combat by +4. There is also a  corresponding increase in the missile's defense. Fast missiles increase the cost and  space of a missile by +25% and require 1 level of refinement to be used.
HELP.LBX          0  8D773      24  ?             Emissions Guidance (EMG)
HELP.LBX          0  8D7DA     215  en            Tracks the warp signature of a vehicle. If the missile penetrates the shields, all damage is applied to the ship's drive, bypassing any armor. Requires 4 times the space and costs 4 times more than regular missiles.
HELP.LBX          0  8DCEE      16                Overloaded (OVR)
HELP.LBX          0  8DD55     174  en            Overloaded increases the warhead strength of torpedoes by +50%, with a  corresponding increase in size and cost by +50%. Overloaded requires 1 level of  refinement to employ.
HELP.LBX          0  8E269      15  ?             Game Popup Exit
HELP.LBX          0  8E2D0     133  en            Clicking here will exit the popup and send you back to the MAIN screen. If you are on the SETTINGS popup, all settings will be saved.
HELP.LBX          0  8E7E4      16  ?             Game Save Button
HELP.LBX          0  8E84B      67  en            Displays the SAVE game screen, where you can save the current game.
HELP.LBX          0  8ED5F      16  ?             Game Load Button
HELP.LBX          0  8EDC6     190  en            Displays the LOAD game screen, where you can load a previously-saved game. Note that in multi-player games, this option is disabled. You may only load multi-players games from the main menu.
HELP.LBX          0  8F2DA      15  ?             New Game Button
HELP.LBX          0  8F341     109  en            Leaves the current game and takes you to the NEW game screen where you will be able to start a the game anew.
HELP.LBX          0  8F855      16  ?             Quit Game Button
HELP.LBX          0  8F8BC      24  en            Quits Master of Orion II
HELP.LBX          0  8FDD0      19  ?             Change Music Volume
HELP.LBX          0  8FE37     321  en            To change the music volume, position the mouse over the bar and press the  left mouse button. The further to the right you press, the higher the  music. You can hold the mouse button down and drag the bar to get a good feel for how loud you want the music. If the bar is placed close to the left, the music will turn off.
HELP.LBX          0  9034B      27  ?             Change Sound Effects Volume
HELP.LBX          0  903B2     355  en            To change the sound effects volume, position the mouse over the bar and  press the left mouse button. The further to the right you press, the  higher the sound effects. You can hold the mouse button down and drag the  bar to get a good feel for how loud you want the sound effects. If the  bar is placed close to the left, the sound effects will turn off.
HELP.LBX          0  908C6      20  ?             Change Game Settings
HELP.LBX          0  9092D      55  en            To change the current game settings, press this button.
HELP.LBX          0  90E41      21  en            Return to Main Screen
HELP.LBX          0  90EA8      47  en            To return to the main screen, press this button
HELP.LBX          0  913BC      18  en            Games to be Loaded
HELP.LBX          0  91423     121  en            To load a game, click on the desired slot. The slot must have a  valid entry. Entries listed as "empty" cannot be loaded.
HELP.LBX          0  91937      11                Cancel Load
HELP.LBX          0  9199E     102  en            If you decide not to load a game, click on this button. You will be sent back to the main GAME screen.
HELP.LBX          0  91EB2      16  ?             Load Game Button
HELP.LBX          0  91F19     229  en            Clicking on the load button will load the game which is highlighted. When  you save a game, the slot number is saved, so that you can "quick-load" the last saved game. You can quick-load using "GLL" keystrokes from the main menu.
HELP.LBX          0  9242D      12                Saving Games
HELP.LBX          0  92494     245  en            Click on a slot to save the game. You will be given the chance to enter a 25 character description. Press ENTER or click on the SAVE button to save the game. If you double-click on the same slot, the game will be saved with the same description.
HELP.LBX          0  929A8      16  ?             Save Game Button
HELP.LBX          0  92A0F     229  en            Clicking on the save button will save the game which is highlighted. When  you save a game, the slot number is saved, so that you can "quick-load" the last saved game. You can quick-save using "GSS" keystrokes from the main menu.
HELP.LBX          0  92F23      19  en            End of Turn Summary
HELP.LBX          0  92F8A     274  en            When this option is ON, the player is given an end-of-turn summary. New ships and buildings built, new discoveries, and player contacts are all  examples of what might appear in the summary. Some information, such as starvation and negative income, will always be dispalyed.
HELP.LBX          0  9349E      16  en            End of Turn Wait
HELP.LBX          0  93505     407  en            When this option is ON, each time the player clicks the TURN button,  one turn is executed. When end-of-turn-wait is OFF, one click of the  TURN button will cause successive turns to go by until "something interesting happens". Any end-of-turn-summary report or GNN report stops the turns from executing automatically. Alternatively, you may click anywhere on the screen to stop the automatic turn sequence.
HELP.LBX          0  93A19      11                Enemy Moves
HELP.LBX          0  93A80      52  en            If ON this option allows you to see the enemy moves.
HELP.LBX          0  93F94      15                Expanding Boxes
HELP.LBX          0  93FFB      84  en            When turned ON, the fleet movement and system display boxes explode out when opened.
HELP.LBX          0  9450F      17  ?             Auto Select Ships
HELP.LBX          0  94576      88  en            When turned ON, this option selects all ships in the fleet when the box is first opened.
HELP.LBX          0  94A8A      10                Animations
HELP.LBX          0  94AF1     124  en            When turned ON, all frames of each animation is played out. To skip the cinematics, and speed up play, turn this option OFF.
HELP.LBX          0  95005      18  ?             Auto Select Colony
HELP.LBX          0  9506C     114  en            When ON, this option bypasses the System Display box and displays colony information for the last colony selected.
HELP.LBX          0  95580      21  ?             Show Relocation Lines
HELP.LBX          0  955E7     123  en            When a star has its ship production relocated to another star, a line will appear, connecting the two stars, in dark green.
HELP.LBX          0  95AFB      22  ?             Show GNN Report Screen
HELP.LBX          0  95B62     175  en            When ON, the reports will be interrupted to show the GNN screen. If you turn this option off, you will still be notified of special events as  part of the normal turn summary.
HELP.LBX          0  96076      30  en            Remove Housing and Trade Goods
HELP.LBX          0  960DD     135  en            When this option is turned on, housing and trade goods will be deleted from the building list if it appears before another application.
HELP.LBX          0  965F1      10                Auto Saves
HELP.LBX          0  96658     272  en            When this option is turned on, every 4 turns the game will be saved to the  last save slot (SAVE10.GAM). When you select "Continue" from the MAIN MENU  screen, this is the game that will be loaded. If you do not wish to save the  game in this manner, turn this option off.
HELP.LBX          0  96B6C      38  ?             Show Only Serious Turn Summary Reports
HELP.LBX          0  96BD3     189  en            When this option is turned on, you will receive a turn summary only if it contains serious reports e.g. starvation, rebellions, and forced scrapping due  to lack of BC's to pay maintenance.
HELP.LBX          0  970E7      15                Ship Initiative
HELP.LBX          0  9714E     230  en            When this option is turned on, ships in tactical combat move in order of their initiative, from highest to lowest. A ship's initiative is equal to its modified beam offense bonus divided by 10 plus the ship's current combat speed.
HELP.LBX          0  97662      21  ?             Accept Options Button
HELP.LBX          0  976C9     115  en            Press the accept button when you are done changing the game options. You will be sent back to the main GAME screen.
HELP.LBX          0  97BDD      17                Population Growth
HELP.LBX          0  97C44     356  en            These bonuses affect the rate at which the population grows.  The amount of population growth is  multiplied by this bonus.  Low population growth rates are a result of shorter life spans, health weakness,  etc., while higher growth rates result from the opposite.  Population growth modifiers include -50% growth  [-4], +50% growth [3], +100% growth [6].
HELP.LBX          0  98158       7                Farming
HELP.LBX          0  981BF     389  en            Farming bonuses affect the amount of food that each farmer can grow.  Races with farming bonuses have  developed advanced agricultural techniques, while races with penalties lack farming aptitude.  Races with  farming penalties cannot be reduced below 1 food per farmer if the world has any life bearing  environment.  Farming modifiers include -1/2 food [-3], +1 food [4], +2 food [7].
HELP.LBX          0  986D3       8                Industry
HELP.LBX          0  9873A     401  en            Industry bonuses affect the amount of production that each factory worker can produce. Races with  industry bonuses have developed advanced manufacturing techniques, while races with penalties lack  manufacturing aptitude.  Races with industrial penalties cannot be reduced below 1 unit of production per  worker.  Industry modifiers include -1 production [-3], +1 production [3], +2 production [6].
HELP.LBX          0  98C4E       7                Science
HELP.LBX          0  98CB5     375  en            Science bonuses affect the amount of research that each scientist  generates.  Races with science bonuses  have developed advanced research techniques, while races with penalties lack scientific aptitude.  Races  with science penalties cannot be reduced below 1 unit of research per scientist.  Science modifiers include   -1 research [-3], +1 research [3], +2 research [6].
HELP.LBX          0  991C9       5                Money
HELP.LBX          0  99230     261  en            Money bonuses affect the amount in credits a population can be taxed.  Races with monetary bonuses  have developed advanced commercial concepts, while races with penalties lack economic skills.  Monetary modifiers include -0.5 BC [-4], +0.5 BC [5], +1 BC [8].
HELP.LBX          0  99744      12                Ship Defense
HELP.LBX          0  997AB     405  en            Ship Defense bonuses decrease the chances of enemy fire hitting you in ship to ship combat.  Races with  bonuses in defense have developed keen evasion senses and have a much better chance of misleading an  attacker.  Penalties, on the other hand, indicate the race has difficulty visualizing complex 3 dimensional  motions.  Defense modifiers include -20 defense [-2], +25 defense [3], +50 defense [7].
HELP.LBX          0  99CBF      11                Ship Attack
HELP.LBX          0  99D26     392  en            Ship Attack bonuses improve the chances of a ship engaged in combat to hit its target.  Races with  bonuses have developed the ability to anticipate a target's motion, and have a much better chance of hitting  the target.  Penalties, on the other hand, indicate a race with poor depth perception and tracking skills.   Attack modifiers include -20 attack [-2], +20 attack [2], +50 attack [4].
HELP.LBX          0  9A23A      13                Ground Combat
HELP.LBX          0  9A2A1     323  en            Ground Combat bonuses affect the combat effectiveness of troops engaged in planetary combat or ship  boarding actions. Higher bonuses are normally indicative of races with extraordinary strength and agility,  while lower combat bonuses indicate the lack thereof.  Ground combat modifiers include -10 [-2], +10 [2],  +20 [4]
HELP.LBX          0  9A7B5       6                Spying
HELP.LBX          0  9A81C     343  en            Spying bonuses affect the sabotage and espionage skills of a race.  Races with high spying bonuses have  specialized disguise abilities or advanced espionage equipment.  All offensive spies sent on missions will  receive the full bonus/penalty, while defensive spies receive one-half the amount.  Modifiers include -10  [-3], +10 [3], +20 [6].
HELP.LBX          0  9AD30      11                Low Gravity
HELP.LBX          0  9AD97     419  en            Cost[-5]:  Races which come from low gravity worlds are considerably weaker than races from  normal-G worlds, and have great difficulty adapting to more intense gravity fields.  Colonists can operate  only in low-G worlds without penalty, and suffer half the heavy-G penalty in normal-G environments.   Finally, Low-G troops are weaker and suffer a -10 ground combat penalty.  Low-G and Heavy-G are  mutually exclusive.
HELP.LBX          0  9B2AB      12                High Gravity
HELP.LBX          0  9B312     403  en            Cost[6]:  Races which come from heavy gravity worlds are considerably hardier than races  from normal-G worlds, and colonists can operate in both heavy-G and normal-G worlds without penalty. In  addition, ground troops can sustain substantially more physical damage than other troops, taking 1 more hit  than normal troops before being slain in ground combats.  Heavy-G and Low-G are mutually exclusive
HELP.LBX          0  9B826       7                Aquatic
HELP.LBX          0  9B88D     282  en            Cost[5]: Aquatic races originated on ocean worlds, and therefore can more easily adapt to primarily  water based environments. Aquatic races treat Tundra and Swamp worlds as Terran and Ocean and  Terran as Gaia environments both for food production and maximum planetary population.
HELP.LBX          0  9BDA1      12                Subterranean
HELP.LBX          0  9BE08     371  en            Cost[6]: Races which were originally subterranean are better adapted to living underground, and  are capable of building expansive complexes below the surface of a planet.  As a result, these races'  maximum population on all worlds is increased by twice that world's size class. Also, subterranean  ground troops receive a +10 combat bonus when defending their colonies.
HELP.LBX          0  9C31C      16  ?             Large Home World
HELP.LBX          0  9C383      81  en            Cost[1]: The home world of your race is large instead of the normal  medium size.
HELP.LBX          0  9C897      15  ?             Rich Home World
HELP.LBX          0  9C8FE     156  en            Cost[2]:  The home world of your race is mineral rich, producing a base 5 production per worker. Rich Home World and Poor Home World are mutually exclusive.
HELP.LBX          0  9CE12      15  ?             Poor Home World
HELP.LBX          0  9CE79     158  en            Cost[-1]:  The home world of your race is mineral poor, producing a base 2  production per worker. Poor Home World and Rich Home World are mutually exclusive.
HELP.LBX          0  9D38D      15                Artifacts World
HELP.LBX          0  9D3F4     112  en            Cost[3]:  The home world of your race has ancient artifacts.  All scientists produce +2 research on this planet.
HELP.LBX          0  9D908      10                Cybernetic
HELP.LBX          0  9D96F     563  en            Cost[4]:  Races which are cybernetic use mechanical appendages and  artificial organs to sustain life. They consume only one half food unit each, and  supplement the other half with one half production unit.  Cybernetics also have an  enhanced ability to repair their ships due to the ease with which they interface with  mechanical devices,  10% of a ship's armor and structure and 5% of a ship's  internal systems will be repaired each round of combat.  All damage to cybernetic  ships is repaired after combat. Cybernetics and Lithovore are mutually exclusive.
HELP.LBX          0  9DE83       9                Lithovore
HELP.LBX          0  9DEEA     229  en            Cost[10]:  These are races which consume rocks instead of food, and thus  can subsist on any planet simply by eating the minerals.  Lithovores do not require  any food whatsoever. Lithovore and Cybernetics are mutually exclusive.
HELP.LBX          0  9E3FE       9                Repulsive
HELP.LBX          0  9E465     484  en            Cost[-6]: Other races find dealing with repulsive races impossible.  Therefore, repulsive races are unable to form any agreements with other races.  They can only use the diplomacy system to declare war and to sue for peace.  Legendary  officers demand an increase of 50% to their cost of hiring to serve with  repulsive races.  Furthermore,  these races assimilate conquered colonists into their population at half the normal rate.  Repulsive and Charismatic are  mutually exclusive.
HELP.LBX          0  9E979      11                Charismatic
HELP.LBX          0  9E9E0     641  en            Cost[3]: Races which are extremely charismatic are quick to make allies and  can almost always talk themselves out of problems.  This ability doubles the effect  of all good diplomatic actions, and halves that of all negative ones.  When proposing  deals, charismatic races have a +50% bonus to their chance of the opponent  accepting. Charismatic races attract more legendary officers and leaders, halving  their hiring cost and increasing the frequency with which heroes ask to be hired.  In  addition, they double the rate at which conquered colonists are assimilated into  their empire.  Charismatic and Repulsive are mutually exclusive.
HELP.LBX          0  9EEF4      10                Uncreative
HELP.LBX          0  9EF5B     268  en            Cost[-4]:  Races which are not particularly creative have great difficulty in  coming up with difficult new technology ideas.  Uncreative races will be able to research only 1 application selected randomly in any field. Uncreative and  Creative are mutually exclusive.
HELP.LBX          0  9F46F       8                Creative
HELP.LBX          0  9F4D6     288  en            Cost[8]:  Races which are creative have little difficulty in coming up with new  technology ideas.  As a result, these races will gain every application in the fields  that they research, instead of only the specific application selected.  Creative and  Uncreative are mutually exclusive.
HELP.LBX          0  9F9EA      24                Environmentally Tolerant
HELP.LBX          0  9FA51     576  en            Cost[10]: These races typically regenerate, or have a  metabolism quite unlike that of a standard humanoid.  Races that are  environmentally tolerant treat all planet environments as Terran for purposes of  maximum population.  Tolerant races also ignore pollution, not spending any  industry to clean it up.  On multi-racial colonies, the proportion of non-tolerant  population to tolerant population determines the amount of pollution that must be  cleaned.  For example, If there are 3 tolerant and 7 non-tolerant population units  7/10 of the pollution must be cleaned up.
HELP.LBX          0  9FF65      17                Fantastic Traders
HELP.LBX          0  9FFCC     320  en            Cost[4]: Races which are fantastic traders possess a keen  understanding of economics and deal making.  They add +25% bonus to the profit  they receive from trade treaties, and receive 1 BC per surplus food created.  In  addition, they receive a +100% bonus to the amount of money they receive for  building trade goods.
HELP.LBX          0  A04E0      10                Telepathic
HELP.LBX          0  A0547     691  en            Cost[6]:  Telepathic races are capable of reading the minds of other beings,  allowing them to exactly isolate the motivations of anyone that they are attempting  to negotiate with. As a result, telepathic races gain a +25% diplomacy bonus when  conducting negations with other races.  Telepaths can also use their mental abilities  for mind control. Telepathic fleets with at least one cruiser or larger ship can mind control a planet instead of bombarding or invading it.  Mind Control  gains ownership of the colony for all purposes instantly assimilating all population.  Finally, telepathic spies are extremely adept at evading enemy  agents and receive a +10% bonus to all spy actions.
HELP.LBX          0  A0A5B       5                Lucky
HELP.LBX          0  A0AC2     216  en            Cost[3]:  Races which are lucky do not suffer from random galactic disasters, and  have a greater chance of benefiting from good events.  Antarans will also have a  tendency to overlook the colonies of lucky players.
HELP.LBX          0  A0FD6      10                Omniscient
HELP.LBX          0  A103D     321  en            Cost[3]:  Omniscient races are visionaries capable of spanning the galaxy  with their minds.  This allows you to know all star system and planetary data  throughout the entire galaxy at the start of the game.  In addition, enemy fleets are  automatically detected, regardless of stealth special abilities or technologies.
HELP.LBX          0  A1551      14                Stealthy Ships
HELP.LBX          0  A15B8     212  en            Cost[4]:  Races with stealthy ships have managed to completely mask  their ships from long range sensors. This special ability has no effect on  ship combat, but their ships will remain unseen on the main screen.
HELP.LBX          0  A1B33     266  en            Cost[5]:  Trans-dimensional beings are capable of folding the fabric  of space with their minds, allowing them to increase the speed at which ships travel  through the galaxy by 2 parsecs per turn. Furthermore, trans-dimensional races gain  +4 to their combat speed.
HELP.LBX          0  A2047       7                Warlord
HELP.LBX          0  A20AE     368  en            Cost[4]:  Races with the warlord special ability have all of their crews function as one  level of experience higher than normal, and the crews have the potential to  eventually become ultra-elites.  Warlords double the rate at which marines and  tanks are built and allows barracks to support twice the normal number of troops.  Each colony produces 2 command points.
HELP.LBX          0  A25C2       6                Feudal
HELP.LBX          0  A2629     680  en            Cost[-4]:  Feudal Governments are ruled by powerful families similiar to  medieval Europe.  Due to the fragmented and warlike nature of these  governments they receive certain benefits and penalties.\x0A ^\x09Ship costs are reduced by 1/3.\x0A ^\x09Planets suffer a -20% morale penalty unless \x09they have a marine or armor barracks.\x0A ^\x09Feudal governments have all research \x09generated by scientists reduced by 50%.\x0A ^\x09Feudal governments assimilate captured population \x09at the rate of 1 population every 8 turns.\x0A ^\x09Feudal populations instantly assimilate when \x09conquered by any other race.  There are always \x09local barons looking out for themselves.
HELP.LBX          0  A2B3D      12                Dictatorship
HELP.LBX          0  A2BA4     524  en            Cost[0]:  In this form of government, one being has absolute power.  All orders and decisions made are  final and the general populace is ruled with an iron hand.  This control confers several benefits and  disadvantages to dictatorships.\x0A ^\x09Defensive agents receive a +10 bonus due to \x09increased internal security.\x0A ^\x09Planets suffer a -20% morale penalty unless \x09they have a marine or armor barracks.\x0A ^\x09Dictatorships assimilate captured population \x09at the rate of 1 population every 8 turns.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  A30B8       9                Democracy
HELP.LBX          0  A311F     648  en            Cost[7]: The people elect representatives to run the government. No single body  of people directly controls the government and the personal freedoms are  greatest of all forms of governments.\x0A ^\x09Defensive agents are penalized -10  due to the emphasis on personal freedoms.\x0A ^\x09Democracies assimilate captured population \x09at the rate of 1 population every 4 turns.\x0A ^\x09Due to the free exchange of ideas all research generated by scientists is increased +50%.\x0A ^\x09The government's concern with promoting trade increases all tax revenues by +50%.\x0A ^\x09Democracies are prohibited from annihilating captured populations.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  A3633      11                Unification
HELP.LBX          0  A369A     814  en            Cost[6]: Only a few races are genetically capable of forming a unified government.   The population exists harmoniously without jealousy, envy or concern for individual advancement.  Each individual works for the improvement of the whole, instead of the desires of  the individual. The unified government is the social equivalent of a colony of bees.\x0A ^\x09Defensive agents receive a +15 bonus due to \x09the lack of traitors.\x0A ^\x09All morale affects and any buildings modifying morale are ignored by unification governments.\x0A ^\x09Unification governments assimilate captured population \x09at the rate of 1 population every 20 turns.\x0A ^\x09Increased productivity results in a +50% bonus to all industrial production.\x0A ^\x09Increased productivity results in a +50% bonus to all food production.\x0A
HELP.LBX          0  A3BAE       5                Clear
HELP.LBX          0  A3C15      47  en            Clears all racial advantages and disadvantages.
HELP.LBX          0  A4129       5                Picks
HELP.LBX          0  A4190     172  en            Each player starts with 10 race development picks with which to design  a race.  Picks left may go negative, but no race will be accepted until  picks left is non-negative.
HELP.LBX          0  A46A4       5                Score
HELP.LBX          0  A470B     149  en            A player's final score in the game will be multiplied by this value.  If all race development picks are not used, a player's score will be increased.
HELP.LBX          0  A4C1F       6                Accept
HELP.LBX          0  A4C86     107  en            Accepts the selected advantages and disadvantages for use in the game and continues on with the game setup.
HELP.LBX          0  A519A       7                ESC key
HELP.LBX          0  A5201     104  en            Pressing the 'ESC' key will abort the race customization process and return to the Race Selection Screen
HELP.LBX          0  A5715      28  ?             Colony Screen : General Help
HELP.LBX          0  A577C     219  en            This is the colony screen. It allows you to view all relavent information  about a single colony. It also allows you to change the production of a  colony, and make any other changes which can occur on the given colony.
HELP.LBX          0  A5C90      18  ?             Status Warning Bar
HELP.LBX          0  A5CF7     207  en            The status warning bar alerts you to potentially dangerous threats to the colony,  such as being blockaded, or a bad random event. Nothing is printed here if  nothing bad is effecting the colony at this time
HELP.LBX          0  A620B      11                Colony Name
HELP.LBX          0  A6272     135  en            This displays the name of the colony including its specialization if any. The specialization of a colony is purely cosmetic in effect.
HELP.LBX          0  A6786      10                Population
HELP.LBX          0  A67ED     675  en             This displays the population of the colony, in the following format: 10,500 k (+ 55). In this case this means 10 million people, or 10 population units, plus 5 hundred  thousand or you are halfway to gaining the next population unit, and the part in parenthesis  is your growth rate.  It can be either positive or negative, indicating respectively  growth or loss of new members of the colonial population. In multiracial colonies this  display becomes less directly indicative of the time you gain your next full population  unit, as each race is growing at a seperate rate, and you are seeing the sum of all the  growth rates added to the number of functioning pop units.
HELP.LBX          0  A6D01      14                System Display
HELP.LBX          0  A6D68     225  en            The Colony Screen System Display shows you the other planets in the system, and if they are colonized, will let you go there by left-clicking on the planet. Clicking on the text will give a  summary description of the planet.
HELP.LBX          0  A727C      18                Current Production
HELP.LBX          0  A72E3     203  en             This window displays the current building or unit being constructed at this  colony, along with a turn counter and a product completion bar showing how  close to completion the product is at this time.
HELP.LBX          0  A77F7      11                BCs Display
HELP.LBX          0  A785E     408  en             This display shows the monetary disposition for this colony, with gold coins showing one BC and stacks representing ten BC's\x0A \x0A BC's can be imported, exported or used locally. These uses are displayed as follows. First comes the amount used here, separated by a space, followed by either exports, which are bright, or by imports, which are darkened. The amounts of each are calculated automatically.
HELP.LBX          0  A7D72      29  en            Government and Morale Display
HELP.LBX          0  A7DD9     342  en             This display show the government, and the current morale for this colony.  First is the Government, being a small version of the government symbol followed by positive morale represented as Smiling/Comedy masks or negative morale represented as Frowning/Drama masks. Each of these represents a 10% change in  the total output of the colony.
HELP.LBX          0  A82ED      11                Jobs Output
HELP.LBX          0  A8354     430  en            The production window displays the output of a colonies workers for each of the three jobs,  Farmers, Workers and Scientists.\x0A \x0A Resources, such as food, can be imported, exported or used locally. These uses are displayed as follows.\x0A First comes the amount used here, separated by a space, followed by either exports, which are bright, or by imports, which are darkened. The amounts of each are calculated automatically.
HELP.LBX          0  A8868       7                Farmers
HELP.LBX          0  A88CF     299  en             Farmers produce food, as displayed by stalks of corn for one unit and bags of corn to display  10 units of food. To import food you must have one freighter per unit of food. Exported food which is not imported is sold for 1/2BCs each(unless you are a fantastic trader, which doubles  this amount).
HELP.LBX          0  A8DE3       7                Workers
HELP.LBX          0  A8E4A     202  en             Workers produce industry which is used to build buildings and units on the production screen. A pick is one unit and a pick on a pile of ore is 10 units. Industry can neither be imported nor exported.
HELP.LBX          0  A935E      10                Scientists
HELP.LBX          0  A93C5     201  en             Scientists produce research, which is used to gain new technology. A test tube represents one  research point, a microscope represents 10 research points. science can neither be imported nor exported
HELP.LBX          0  A98D9      22  ?             Population Job Display
HELP.LBX          0  A9940     129  en             This display show exactly how many population units (1,000,000 people each) are in each given job, Farmer, Worker or Scientist.
HELP.LBX          0  A9E54      13                Units Display
HELP.LBX          0  A9EBB     168  en             This display shows the number of infantry or armor you have at this colony.  Infantry can either be Normal or Powersuited, and Armor can be either Tanks or Battleoids
HELP.LBX          0  AA3CF      13                Change Button
HELP.LBX          0  AA436     120  en             This button takes you to the Colony Building Queue Screen, where you can change what the colony is currently producing
HELP.LBX          0  AA94A      10                Buy Button
HELP.LBX          0  AA9B1     170  en             This button will let you spend BCs to accelerate the production of the currently produced product, assuming you currently have enough BCs in your reserve to do the job.
HELP.LBX          0  AAEC5      14                Leaders Button
HELP.LBX          0  AAF2C      88  en             This button will take you to the Leaders Screen, where you hire move and fire leaders.
HELP.LBX          0  AB440      13                Return Button
HELP.LBX          0  AB4A7      43  en            Allows you to return to the previous screen
HELP.LBX          0  AB9BB      14                Buildings List
HELP.LBX          0  ABA22     247  en            Shows a list of all the buildings you are currently able to build  at this colony. To add a building to the Queue, left click on it once.  Buildings already in the queue are drawn darkened and can be clicked  on again to remove them from the queue
HELP.LBX          0  ABF36      23  ?             Current Product Picture
HELP.LBX          0  ABF9D      94  en            Shows the picture of the top element of the queue, or of the product  currently being scanned.
HELP.LBX          0  AC4B1      23  ?             Current Product Summary
HELP.LBX          0  AC518     128  en            Shows the name, cost and other summary information for the top element  of the queue, or of the product currently being scanned.
HELP.LBX          0  ACA2C      14                Military Units
HELP.LBX          0  ACA93     125  en            Shows the list of all military and civilian units you can build at the colony.  Left clicking on them adds them to the queue.
HELP.LBX          0  ACFA7      27  ?             Current Product Description
HELP.LBX          0  AD00E      99  en            Shows the description for the top element of the queue, or of the product  currently being scanned.
HELP.LBX          0  AD522      13                Product Queue
HELP.LBX          0  AD589     661  en            Shows up to seven buildings or units which are either currently being built,  or waiting their turn to be built.\x0AClicking on a entry in the queue selects it. Clicking again on a selected entry deletes the entry. \x0AClicking on another entry, while one is selected,  moves the current entry to the spot immediatly below the clicked on entry, compacting the queue first if applicable. Clicking on a building or unit, while an entry is selected, adds the  product to the queue, if there is space, immediately above the current  entry, unless it is a building which is already in the queue, in which  case it deletes it, and leaves the selected entry selected.
HELP.LBX          0  ADA9D      17  ?             Auto Build Button
HELP.LBX          0  ADB04     241  en            This button, if active, shows that the computer is currently making all  decisions about which building to build at the current colony. If no building is chosen,  trade goods will be selected. Autobuild will never build a ship or other unit.
HELP.LBX          0  AE018      12                Refit Button
HELP.LBX          0  AE07F      28  en            Calles the refit ship popup.
HELP.LBX          0  AE593      13                Design Button
HELP.LBX          0  AE5FA     158  en            Sets the cursor to the 'Which Ship' cursor, allowing you to click on  a ship in the units list and goto the Design screen the change the  design in that slot.
HELP.LBX          0  AEB0E      19  ?             Repeat Build Button
HELP.LBX          0  AEB75     181  en            Sets the cursor to the 'What' cursor, allowing you to select a unit to be built repeatedly, until either you delete it from the queue, or the  rules do not allow another to be built
HELP.LBX          0  AF089       9                Ok Button
HELP.LBX          0  AF0F0      75  en            Allows you return to the previous screen, saving any changes you have made.
HELP.LBX          0  AF604      36  ?             Building Queue Screen : General Help
HELP.LBX          0  AF66B     117  en            This screen allows you to make any an all building and unit choice decisions you desire to make for the given colony.
HELP.LBX          0  AFB7F      36  ?             Colony Summary Screen : General Help
HELP.LBX          0  AFBE6      26  en            The Colony Summary Screen!
HELP.LBX          0  B00FA      16  ?             Scroll Up Button
HELP.LBX          0  B0161      22  en            It scrolls the list up
HELP.LBX          0  B0675      19  ?             Name Display Window
HELP.LBX          0  B06DC      29  en            Shows the name of the colony
HELP.LBX          0  B0BF0      22  ?             Farmers Display Window
HELP.LBX          0  B0C57      51  en            Shows the number of farmers. Farmers produce food.
HELP.LBX          0  B116B      22  ?             Workers Display Window
HELP.LBX          0  B11D2      54  en            Shows the number of workers. Workers produce industry.
HELP.LBX          0  B16E6      25  ?             Scientists Display Window
HELP.LBX          0  B174D      60  en            Shows the number of Scientists. Scientists produce research.
HELP.LBX          0  B1C61      25  ?             Production Display Window
HELP.LBX          0  B1CC8      62  en            Shows the amount of production of the currently scanned colony
HELP.LBX          0  B21DC      11                Buy Buttons
HELP.LBX          0  B2243      66  en            Allows you to attempt to purchase the current product in the queue
HELP.LBX          0  B2757      17  ?             Scroll Slider Bar
HELP.LBX          0  B27BE      32  en            Allows you to scroll the list up
HELP.LBX          0  B2CD2      18  ?             Scroll Down Button
HELP.LBX          0  B2D39      72  en            Allows you to scroll down the list of colonies which you currently have.
HELP.LBX          0  B324D      26  ?             Colony Info Summary Window
HELP.LBX          0  B32B4      61  en            Lists information about the colony you are currently scanning
HELP.LBX          0  B37C8      30  ?             Colony Scanned Products Window
HELP.LBX          0  B382F      90  en            Shows the icons for the number of each kind of production for the currently scanned colony
HELP.LBX          0  B3D43      17  ?             Galaxy Map Window
HELP.LBX          0  B3DAA     105  en            Shows the galaxy map, the currently scanned star, the source and destination stars when moving colonists.
HELP.LBX          0  B42BE      18  ?             Empire Info Window
HELP.LBX          0  B4325      52  en            Shows the summary information for your entire empire
HELP.LBX          0  B4839      19  ?             Sort By Name Button
HELP.LBX          0  B48A0      59  en            Allows you to sort the colonies by the name of the colonies
HELP.LBX          0  B4DB4      18  ?             Sort By Pop Button
HELP.LBX          0  B4E1B      65  en            Allows you to sort the colonies by the population of the colonies
HELP.LBX          0  B532F      19  ?             Sort By Food Button
HELP.LBX          0  B5396      78  en            Allows you to sort the colonies by the amount of food produced on the colonies
HELP.LBX          0  B58AA      23  ?             Sort By Industry Button
HELP.LBX          0  B5911      82  en            Allows you to sort the colonies by the amount of industry produced on the colonies
HELP.LBX          0  B5E25      22  ?             Sort By Science Button
HELP.LBX          0  B5E8C      82  en            Allows you to sort the colonies by the amount of research produced on the colonies
HELP.LBX          0  B63A0      24  ?             Sort By Producing Button
HELP.LBX          0  B6407      78  en            Allows you to sort the colonies by the products being produced on the colonies
HELP.LBX          0  B691B      17  ?             Sort By BC Button
HELP.LBX          0  B6982      78  en            Allows you to sort the colonies by the amount of BC's produced on the colonies
HELP.LBX          0  B6E96      31  ?             Refit Ship Popup : General Help
HELP.LBX          0  B6EFD      80  en            Allows you to select a ship from the list of ship which are at the star to refit
HELP.LBX          0  B7411       9                Ship List
HELP.LBX          0  B7478      75  en            Shows the list of ship which are at this star and available to be refitted.
HELP.LBX          0  B798C      16  ?             Ship Info Window
HELP.LBX          0  B79F3      71  en            Shows the information for the ship which you are currently pointing at.
HELP.LBX          0  B7F07      13                Cancel Button
HELP.LBX          0  B7F6E      46  en            Allows you to exit without making any changes.
HELP.LBX          0  B8482      25  ?             Population Display Window
HELP.LBX          0  B84E9      43  en            show the current pops for the given colony.
HELP.LBX          0  B89FD      30  ?             Transport Popup : General Help
HELP.LBX          0  B8A64     119  en            This screen allows you to quickly move population from one colony to another without going to the colony summary screen
HELP.LBX          0  B8F78      27  ?             Colony Ground Combat Screen
HELP.LBX          0  B8FDF     226  en            The Colony Ground Combat Screen allows you to watch the invasion of a planet occur,   waiting or clicking once begins the combat, clicking again accelerates it to the end,   after it has ended, clicking again exits the screen
HELP.LBX          0  B94F3      14                Attack Summary
HELP.LBX          0  B955A      61  en            Shows the bonuses and units available on this plant to invade
HELP.LBX          0  B9A6E      14                Defend Summary
HELP.LBX          0  B9AD5      78  en            Shows the bonuses and units available on this plant to defend against invaders
HELP.LBX          0  B9FE9      23  ?             Occupation Policy Popup
HELP.LBX          0  BA050     105  en            The occupation policy popup allows you choose to annihilate all the colonists which are not of your race.
HELP.LBX          0  BA564      10                Galaxy Age
HELP.LBX          0  BA5CB     285  en             Left clicking here allows you to cycle through the  different galaxy ages, mineral rich, normal and organic rich. Mineral rich increases the chance of planets which have mineral  resources and decreases the chance of generating ones which create food. Organic rich does the opposite.
HELP.LBX          0  BAADF      15  ?             New Game Screen
HELP.LBX          0  BAB46      89  en            The New Game screen allows you to select the options for the game you are about to begin.
HELP.LBX          0  BB05A      15                Game Difficulty
HELP.LBX          0  BB0C1     128  en            Clicking here allows you to choose between the various levels of the game difficulty, Tutor, Ease, Average, Hard and Impossible.
HELP.LBX          0  BB5D5      11                Galaxy Size
HELP.LBX          0  BB63C     183  en            Clicking here allows you to choose between the various levels of galaxy size, which effect the number of stars and overall  volume of space included in the galaxy about to be created
HELP.LBX          0  BBB50      21  ?             Tech Level : Advanced
HELP.LBX          0  BBBB7     384  en            Clicking here allows you to choose between the various levels of starting technology. Prewarp, Average, and Advanced.\x0A\x0A Advanced Civilization starts you with a larger empire, filling up your  share of the galaxy depending on size and number of players.  It also starts you with several levels of technological advancement,  and a fleet which uses up all of your command points.
HELP.LBX          0  BC0CB      20  ?             Tech Level : Average
HELP.LBX          0  BC132     301  en            Clicking here allows you to choose between the various levels of starting technology. Prewarp, Average, and Advanced.\x0A\x0A Average Civilization starts you at a single star, on the very cusp of interstellar travel. You begin with two scouts and a colony ship, and only the most basic of technology.
HELP.LBX          0  BC646      20  ?             Tech Level : Prewarp
HELP.LBX          0  BC6AD     306  en            Clicking here allows you to choose between the various levels of starting technology. Prewarp, Average, and Advanced.\x0A\x0A Prewarp Civilization starts you at a single star, with no ships, and even  the most basic of technology must be researched before you can build  even your first interstellar ship.
HELP.LBX          0  BCBC1      10                Tech Level
HELP.LBX          0  BCC28     117  en            Clicking here allows you to choose between the various levels of starting technology. Prewarp, Average, and Advanced.
HELP.LBX          0  BD13C      17  en            Number Of Players
HELP.LBX          0  BD1A3      97  en            Clicking here allows you to choose the number of players, including yourself, to be in the game.
HELP.LBX          0  BD6B7      20  ?             Random Events Button
HELP.LBX          0  BD71E      62  en            Clicking here allows you to turn on and off the Random Events
HELP.LBX          0  BDC32      22  ?             Tactical Combat Button
HELP.LBX          0  BDC99     219  en            Clicking here allows you to change between Tactical and Strategic Combat. Strategic combat means that the computer will play out any combats for you, returning you the results, and design all the ships for you as well.
HELP.LBX          0  BE1AD      22  ?             Antarans Attack Button
HELP.LBX          0  BE214      89  en            Clicking here allows you to turn on and off the Antarans attacking players in this game.
HELP.LBX          0  BE728      13                Accept Button
HELP.LBX          0  BE78F      83  en            Clicking here allows you to accept the current settings and continue with the game.
HELP.LBX          0  BECA3      14                Cancel Button
HELP.LBX          0  BED0A      46  en            Allows you to exit without making any changes.
HELP.LBX          0  BF21E      21  ?             Player Attacked Popup
HELP.LBX          0  BF285      61  en            This popup informs you when a player is attacked and by whom.
HELP.LBX          0  BF799      27  ?             New Colony Confirmation Box
HELP.LBX          0  BF800     121  en            This popup gives you summary information on the potential colony and  allows you to decide whether or not to colonize it.
HELP.LBX          0  BFD14      14  ?             Tax Rate Popup
HELP.LBX          0  BFD7B     164  en            This popup allows you to set your tax rate. The percentage value of the  tax rate is the percentage of all production from all your colonies to be  turned into cash
HELP.LBX          0  C028F      21  ?             Dragon New Star Popup
HELP.LBX          0  C02F6     137  en            This popup allows you to bribe a space dragon not to attack your system,  and to select what other system you would like it to goto next.
HELP.LBX          0  C080A      26  ?             New System Discovery Popup
HELP.LBX          0  C0871     119  en            This popup tells shows you all the relevant information about a given newly explored system, including specials if any.
HELP.LBX          0  C0D85      22  ?             Planet Selection Popup
HELP.LBX          0  C0DEC     343  en             This popup allows you to select a planet to perform one of the following operations on, build a new colony, outpost, artificial planet, or drop troops on a planet to reinforce  its defenses. If you are building from a ship, and hit cancel, you will not be prompted again to build here until you hit the appropriate button on the fleet popup.
HELP.LBX          0  C1300      25  ?             Officer Information Popup
HELP.LBX          0  C1367     210  en             This popup informs you of the occurence of one of several things. It can tell you about  when an officer gains a level, or when a marooned officer joins you or fails to join because you have  no room for it.
HELP.LBX          0  C187B      29  ?             Combat Colony Selection Popup
HELP.LBX          0  C18E2     282  en            This popup allows you to select a colony or fleet to attack, or to select not  to attack at all. Hitting cancel chooses not to attack, and you will not  be prompted again until either the situation at the star changes (new ships etc) or you hit the attack button on the fleet. popup
HELP.LBX          0  C1DF6      19  ?             Audience: Main Menu
HELP.LBX          0  C1E5D     120  en            Select a category of diplomatic action from the menu of choices. Selections that are presently unavailable are darkened.
HELP.LBX          0  C2371      14                Propose Treaty
HELP.LBX          0  C23D8      99  it            Suggest forming an alliance, peace treaty, trade treaty, research treaty, or non-aggression treaty.
HELP.LBX          0  C28EC      12                Break Treaty
HELP.LBX          0  C2953      38  ?             Cancel an existing treaty or alliance.
HELP.LBX          0  C2E67       6                Demand
HELP.LBX          0  C2ECE      64  en            Require this Empire to perform a specific action to appease you.
HELP.LBX          0  C33E2      10                Offer Gift
HELP.LBX          0  C3449      70  en            Offer a tribute, tech, or star system to appease the selected Emperor.
HELP.LBX          0  C395D      13                Exchange Tech
HELP.LBX          0  C39C4      86  en            Suggest trading an application you have discovered for one the selected Race posesses.
HELP.LBX          0  C3ED8      11                Declare War
HELP.LBX          0  C3F3F      46  en            Formal declaration of war against this Empire.
HELP.LBX          0  C4453       9                Surrender
HELP.LBX          0  C44BA      57  en            Turn control of your Empire over to the selected Emperor.
HELP.LBX          0  C49CE      17                Audience: Goodbye
HELP.LBX          0  C4A35      23  en            Exits from this screen.
HELP.LBX          0  C4F49      13                Treaties Menu
HELP.LBX          0  C4FB0      65  en            Select a treaty to offer. Unavailable selections appear darkened.
HELP.LBX          0  C54C4      18  ?             Offer Trade Treaty
HELP.LBX          0  C552B     174  en            A Trade treaty generates income based on the minimum of the two empires population.  The  break-even point is 5 turns and it will take at least 10 turns to reach the maximum.
HELP.LBX          0  C5A3F      21  ?             Offer Research Treaty
HELP.LBX          0  C5AA6     186  en            A Research treaty generates research points based on the minimum of the two empires population.  The  break-even point is 5 turns and it will take at least 10 turns to reach the maximum.
HELP.LBX          0  C5FBA      18  ?             Offer Peace Treaty
HELP.LBX          0  C6021      51  en            Propose an end to the current war with this Empire.
HELP.LBX          0  C6535      27  it            Offer Non-Aggression Treaty
HELP.LBX          0  C659C      68  en            Propose that neither race will mount an offensive against the other.
HELP.LBX          0  C6AB0      14                Offer Alliance
HELP.LBX          0  C6B17     134  en            Propose that neither race will mount an offensive against the other.  Allies also get to  use each others colonies for range purposes.
HELP.LBX          0  C702B      24  ?             Break Treaties Selection
HELP.LBX          0  C7092      82  en            Select the treaty that you wish to cancel. Unavailable selections appear darkened.
HELP.LBX          0  C75A6      18  ?             Break Trade Treaty
HELP.LBX          0  C760D      46  en            End the current Trade Treaty with this Empire.
HELP.LBX          0  C7B21      21  ?             Break Research Treaty
HELP.LBX          0  C7B88      49  en            End the current Research Treaty with this Empire.
HELP.LBX          0  C809C      20  ?             Break Tribute Treaty
HELP.LBX          0  C8103      48  en            End the current Tribute Treaty with this Empire.
HELP.LBX          0  C8617      27  it            Break Non-Aggression Treaty
HELP.LBX          0  C867E      55  en            End the current Non-Aggression Treaty with this Empire.
HELP.LBX          0  C8B92      14                Break Alliance
HELP.LBX          0  C8BF9      42  en            End the current Alliance with this Empire.
HELP.LBX          0  C910D      11                Demand Menu
HELP.LBX          0  C9174      79  en            Select the action you require to be taken. Unavailable options appear darkened.
HELP.LBX          0  C9688      22  en            Demand: Declare War On
HELP.LBX          0  C96EF      65  en            Choose a third race you wish this Emperor to declare war against.
HELP.LBX          0  C9C03      23  en            Demand: Make Peace With
HELP.LBX          0  C9C6A     124  en            Choose a third race you wish this Emperor to sign a peace treaty with.  This option is  not available in multi-player games.
HELP.LBX          0  CA17E      27  en            Demand: Break Alliance With
HELP.LBX          0  CA1E5      69  en            Choose a third race you wish this Emperor to end their alliance with.
HELP.LBX          0  CA6F9      25  ?             Demand: Annual 5% Tribute
HELP.LBX          0  CA760      76  en            Require this Emperor to pay you an annual sum equal to 5% of their treasury.
HELP.LBX          0  CAC74      26  ?             Demand: Annual 10% Tribute
HELP.LBX          0  CACDB      77  en            Require this Emperor to pay you an annual sum equal to 10% of their treasury.
HELP.LBX          0  CB1EF      19  ?             Demand: Stop Spying
HELP.LBX          0  CB256      61  en            Require this Emperor to remove all spies from your territory.
HELP.LBX          0  CB76A      18                Demand: Technology
HELP.LBX          0  CB7D1      56  en            Choose an application you want this Emperor to give you.
HELP.LBX          0  CBCE5      24  ?             Demand: Surrender System
HELP.LBX          0  CBD4C      54  en            Choose a star sytem you want this Emperor to give you.
HELP.LBX          0  CC260      35  en            Demand: Remove Fleet From My System
HELP.LBX          0  CC2C7      72  en            Call for this Emperor to remove all ships in orbit around your colonies.
HELP.LBX          0  CC7DB      15  ?             Offer Gift Menu
HELP.LBX          0  CC842      67  en            Select a gift to give this Emperor to improve diplomatic relations.
HELP.LBX          0  CCD56      24  ?             Offer: Annual 5% Tribute
HELP.LBX          0  CCDBD      60  en            Pay this Emperor an annual sum equal to 5% of your treasury.
HELP.LBX          0  CD2D1      25  ?             Offer: Annual 10% Tribute
HELP.LBX          0  CD338      61  en            Pay this Emperor an annual sum equal to 10% of your treasury.
HELP.LBX          0  CD84C      22  ?             Offer: Technology Gift
HELP.LBX          0  CD8B3      52  en            Offer a technology application to give this Emperor.
HELP.LBX          0  CDDC7      18  ?             Offer: System Gift
HELP.LBX          0  CDE2E      41  en            Offer a star system to give this Emperor.
HELP.LBX          0  CE342      12                Offer: Money
HELP.LBX          0  CE3A9      46  en            Offer this Emperor a specific amount of money.
HELP.LBX          0  CE8BD      25  ?             Technology Gift Selection
HELP.LBX          0  CE924      67  en            Select which technology application you want to offer this Emperor.
HELP.LBX          0  CEE38      28  ?             Offer: System Gift Selection
HELP.LBX          0  CEE9F      77  en            Select which star system you wish to give this Emperor using the reduced map.
HELP.LBX          0  CF3B3      32  en            Demand: Declare War On Selection
HELP.LBX          0  CF41A     103  en            Choose which race you wish this Emperor to declare war against. Unavailable selections appear darkened.
HELP.LBX          0  CF92E      33  en            Demand: Make Peace With Selection
HELP.LBX          0  CF995     108  en            Choose which race you wish this Emperor to sign a peace treaty with. Unavailable selections appear darkened.
HELP.LBX          0  CFEA9      37  en            Demand: Break Alliance With Selection
HELP.LBX          0  CFF10     107  en            Choose which race you wish this Emperor to end their alliance with. Unavailable selections appear darkened.
HELP.LBX          0  D0424      28  ?             Demand: Technology Selection
HELP.LBX          0  D048B      59  en            Choose which application you want this Emperor to give you.
HELP.LBX          0  D099F      34  ?             Demand: Surrender System Selection
HELP.LBX          0  D0A06      80  en            Choose which star sytem you want this Emperor to give you using the reduced map.
HELP.LBX          0  D0F1A      23  ?             Exchange Tech Selection
HELP.LBX          0  D0F81     123  en            Choose which technology you wish this Emperor to give you. Choose 'next page' and 'previous page' to scroll though the list
HELP.LBX          0  D1495      22  ?             Exchange Tech Response
HELP.LBX          0  D14FC      89  en            This Emperor is willing to give you this application in exchange for the one you offered.
HELP.LBX          0  D1A10      22                Surrender Verification
HELP.LBX          0  D1A77      81  en            Indicate whether you really wish to turn your entire Empire over to this Emperor.
HELP.LBX          0  D1F8B      16                Diplomacy Cancel
HELP.LBX          0  D1FF2      18  en            Exits this screen.
HELP.LBX          0  D2506      24  ?             Declare War Verification
HELP.LBX          0  D256D      59  en            Indicate whether you really wish to declare on this Empire.
HELP.LBX          0  D2A81      22  ?             Offer Money: Selection
HELP.LBX          0  D2AE8      55  en            Select the amount, in BC, you wish to give this Empire.
HELP.LBX          0  D2FFC      29  ?             Offer: Offer System Selection
HELP.LBX          0  D3063      77  en            Choose which star sytem you want to offer this Emperor using the reduced map.
HELP.LBX          0  D3577      14                Options Button
HELP.LBX          0  D35DE     153  en            Pressing the options button will slide up a panel that allows the setting of  various combat options and giving self-destruct orders to the current ship.
HELP.LBX          0  D3AF2      20  ?             Current Ship Display
HELP.LBX          0  D3B59     318  en            This window displays the currently active ship.  Left clicking anywhere in this  window will center the main viewport on the current ship. The stars at the upper left of the ship display window denote crew levels.  If there is a leader present on this ship there will be a (L) in the upper right corner of the display.
HELP.LBX          0  D406D      10                Damage Bar
HELP.LBX          0  D40D4     197  en            The blue, red, and yellow bars display types of damage to the ship.  The blue  bar shows damage to armor, the red bar shows damage to structure, and the yellow bar shows damage to internal systems.
HELP.LBX          0  D45E8      11                Map Display
HELP.LBX          0  D464F     231  en            The map display shows the entire area of the combat.  Ships are shown as blips in the appropriate color.  Missiles and fighters are displayed as white dots. Left clicking anywhere on the map centers the main viewport on that point.
HELP.LBX          0  D4B63      21  ?             Missile Warning Panel
HELP.LBX          0  D4BCA     287  en            The missile warning appears when the current ship has been ordered to make a move that will allow enemy missiles to hit the ship.  Clicking in this box will remove  the warning and allow the current ship to continue moving.  This warning can be turned completely off on the options menu.
HELP.LBX          0  D50DE      24  ?             Internals/Target Display
HELP.LBX          0  D5145     229  en            Generally, this display shows the current damage points of the major internal systems and the remaining movement points of the current ship.  When the mouse pointer is over a ship, this display changes to show target information.
HELP.LBX          0  D5659      11                Auto Button
HELP.LBX          0  D56C0     347  en            This button gives control of all your ships to the computer AI.  The combat  will proceed without any input from you.  Clicking anywhere on the screen will return control of your ships back to you after the current ship has finished its turn.\x0A NOTE: Your ships will not retreat from combat under any circumstances while  under computer control.
HELP.LBX          0  D5BD4      11                Scan Button
HELP.LBX          0  D5C3B     222  en            Clicking this button toggles scan mode on and off.  While in scan mode clicking on any ship will bring up a detailed display of that ship.  Moving the current viewport is the only other command accepted while in scan mode.
HELP.LBX          0  D614F      12                Board Button
HELP.LBX          0  D61B6     327  en            Clicking this button toggles boarding mode on and off.  While in boarding mode clicking on an enemy ship will cause the currently active ship to attempt to board it.  To board an enemy ship it must be immobilized due to damage to its drive or  the effect of tractor beams or the current ship must be equipped with transporters.
HELP.LBX          0  D66CA      14                Retreat Button
HELP.LBX          0  D6731     323  en            This button will give the current ship orders to retreat.  The retreat from combat  will take place at the start of your next turn.  If you win the combat retreated ships will rejoin your fleet.  If you lose, retreated ships will be given orders  to move to your nearest colony or outpost, even if it is in the same system.
HELP.LBX          0  D6C45      11                Wait Button
HELP.LBX          0  D6CAC     118  en            This button cycles to the next active ship in your fleet, and leaves the current active ship still in the active list.
HELP.LBX          0  D71C0      11                Done Button
HELP.LBX          0  D7227     115  en            This button cycles to the next active ship in your fleet, and removes the current active ship from the active list.
HELP.LBX          0  D773B      15                Weapons Display
HELP.LBX          0  D77A2     485  en            Displays weapons on current ship.  Right clicking on an individual weapon will  display information on that weapon. Weapon status is displayed by color:\x0A Green: this weapon will is available to fire.\x0A Orange: this weapon is on standby. It will not fire the next time the ship fires,  but will then revert to normal status.\x0A Red: this weapon has been turned off. It will not fire until manually turned on.  Point  Defense weapons will still fire on missiles before they impact.
HELP.LBX          0  D7CB6       6                Alkari
HELP.LBX          0  D7D1D     408  en            The Alkari are an avian race which have descended from great flying reptiles.  Alkari pilots  are reared from a young age on the dynamics of 3-dimensional motion.  As a result the  Alkari boast superior pilots, gaining a +50 defensive bonus in space combat. Furthermore,  the Alkari homeworld was once colonized by the Orions, and still possesses ancient  artifacts. The Alkari have a dictatorial government.
HELP.LBX          0  D8231       8                Bulrathi
HELP.LBX          0  D8298     426  en            The Bulrathi are a large bear-like people that possess tremendous strength and hardiness.  The Bulrathi home world is a heavy gravity planet, making the race exceptionally  strong and able to perform in all heavy-G worlds without penalty. Due to their aggressive nature they recieve a +20 bonus to offense in space combat. In addition, the Bulrathi  have a +10 bonus in ground combat and have a dictatorial form of government.
HELP.LBX          0  D87AC       7                Darloks
HELP.LBX          0  D8813     290  en            The Darlok people are shape shifters, who can assume almost any humanoid form.  As a  result, all Darlok spies gain a +20 bonus to any spy mission.  Furthermore, Darloks have  the ability to render their ships invisible to long range detection.  They have a dictatorial  form of government.
HELP.LBX          0  D8D27       8                Elerians
HELP.LBX          0  D8D8E     742  en            The Elerian people are humanoid, with strong angular facial features, almost elf-like. They  follow an order of female mystics that are omniscient and know about all of the planets  when the game begins, and can always sense the presence of enemy fleets, regardless of  range. Furthermore, the mystics can see slightly into the future giving them tactical  advantages in space combat, adding +20 to their offense and +25 to their defense. The greatest  of the Elerian mystics are telepathic, allowing them to mind control and automatically  capture undefended enemy worlds and gain immediate use of captured ships. In addition, their  telepathic ability grants the Elerians +10% to all spy actions. Elerians have a feudal form  of government.
HELP.LBX          0  D92A2       7                Gnolams
HELP.LBX          0  D9309     709  en            The Gnolams are a dwarf-like people, with a society that focuses almost exclusively on  monetary gains.  As a result, the Gnolams are fantastic traders, doubling the gains they  make from trade treaties.  The capitalistic nature of the Gnolam is so intense that each  Gnolam generates a bonus of +1 BC per  population. Gnolams are lucky, and will never be  affected by random disasters, and are more likely to be affected by good events.  The  Gnolams are small in stature and come from a Low-G homeworld and suffer from significant  industry and farming penalties on normal and heavy-G worlds, as well as having a  -10  penalty to all ground combat engagements. Gnolams have a dictatorial form of government.
HELP.LBX          0  D981D       6                Humans
HELP.LBX          0  D9884     244  en            Humans are the most charismatic deal makers of the game.  They gain a +50% diplomacy  bonus when dealing with other races and pay half price to hire legendary officers and  leaders. Humans are the only race with a democratic form of government.
HELP.LBX          0  D9D98       8                Klackons
HELP.LBX          0  D9DFF     496  en            The Klackons are an insectoid people who are completely satisfied with their life.  Their hive  mind allows communication to pass swiftly and effectively, with each worker acting with  great conviction, operating as one. As a result, Klackons are the only race with a unified  government. In addition, Klackons are extremely industrious workers, adding +1 to both  their food and industry production. Unfortunately,they are uncreative and have  great difficulty in coming up with new technologies
HELP.LBX          0  DA313       7                Meklars
HELP.LBX          0  DA37A     564  en            The Meklars are a cybernetic race that have become extremely dependent on their  cybernetic exoskeletons, to the point that their bodies have atrophied to small fragile  frames.  Unlike other races, Meklars consume 1/2 production and 1/2 food each, rounded  up. Their cybernetic interfaces allow them to completely repair their ships  after combat. In addition 10% of their ship's structure and 5% of their ship's internal  systems are repaired each round of combat. Meklar factory workers produce +2 production each. Meklars have a dictatorial form of government.
HELP.LBX          0  DA88E       7                Mrrshan
HELP.LBX          0  DA8F5     461  en            The Mrrshan are a cat-like race with keen senses, giving them  a +50 to hit bonus to all of  their ship beam attacks. The Mrrshan possess a strict warrior code and are warlords by  nature, doubling the start, rate and maximum number of troops and armor that can be  stationed on a planet. Furthermore, they increase the level of their crew and their legendary officers and leaders by one. They have a mineral rich homeworld and a dictatorial form of government.
HELP.LBX          0  DAE09       7                Psilons
HELP.LBX          0  DAE70     388  en            The Psilons are a delicate race of brilliant researchers from a Low-G home world. Each Psilon scientist produces 2 more research than the galactic norm. In  addition, the Psilons are very creative, and they never ignore a potential  avenue of research. Thus, all technologies are available to their scientists. Their large home world doesn't hurt either. They are ruled by a Dictatorship.
HELP.LBX          0  DB384       6                Sakkra
HELP.LBX          0  DB3EB     532  en            The Sakkra are a race of reptiles with impressive regenerative capabilities.   As a result, their population grows at twice the normal rate.  They are  subterranean, living both under and above the surface of a planet, increasing  the maximum population a planet can support by twice the planet's size. The Sakkra  are very good at agriculture giving them a bonus of +1 food per farmer, but somewhat  inept at spying with a -10 to all spying activities. The Sakkra come from a  large home world and have a feudal form of government.
HELP.LBX          0  DB8FF       9                Silicoids
HELP.LBX          0  DB966     450  en            The Silicoids are crystalline beings that are lithovores, eating minerals instead of food.  They  are environmentally tolerant but suffer from half the standard population growth rate.  Silcoids are also repulsive, incapable of effectively comprehending the nature  of other beings, making it extremely difficult to negotiate with other races and doubling the cost of hiring legendary officers and leaders. They have a dictatorial form of government.
HELP.LBX          0  DBE7A      10                Trilarians
HELP.LBX          0  DBEE1     481  en            Trilarians are aquatic based life forms and as such they treat all tundra and swamp worlds as ocean and ocean and terrans as gaias. Their homeworld is an ocean world and therefore can support more colonists and  grows 3 food per farmer. Trilarians are also trans-dimensional and can fold space with their  minds, increasing the speed of their ships on the galactic map by 2 parsecs per turn and increasing their combat speed by 4.  Trilarians have a dictatorial form of government.
HELP.LBX          0  DC3F5       6                Custom
HELP.LBX          0  DC45C      82  en            Allows the player to completely customize all racial advantages and disadvantages.
HELP.LBX          0  DC970      18  ?             Race Select Screen
HELP.LBX          0  DC9D7      71  en            Select the race you will play or choose custom to design your own race.
HELP.LBX          0  DCEEB      15  en            Continue A Game
HELP.LBX          0  DCF52     175  en            By selecting "Continue Game", you can continue with the previously-played game at the point it was last saved. Every four turns the game is saved  automatically to SAVE10.GAM.
HELP.LBX          0  DD466      11  en            Load A Game
HELP.LBX          0  DD4CD     190  en            "Load Game" will show a menu of possible saves, from which you will  select the game you wish to continue. If no games have been saved, this option will appear dull and will be unselectable.
HELP.LBX          0  DD9E1      16  en            Start A New Game
HELP.LBX          0  DDA48     133  en            This option will allow you to start a new game. After generating a new  universe, the game will be automatically saved to SAVE10.GAM.
HELP.LBX          0  DDF5C      25  ?             Multi Player Game Options
HELP.LBX          0  DDFC3      87  en            If you wish to play Master Of Orion II with multiple human players, select this option.
HELP.LBX          0  DE4D7      12  en            Hall Of Fame
HELP.LBX          0  DE53E      89  en            To show a list of the "elite" Master of Orion II players, select the Hall Of Fame option.
HELP.LBX          0  DEA52      23  en            Quit Master Of Orion II
HELP.LBX          0  DEAB9      80  en            Selecting this option will quit the game and return you to the operating system.
HELP.LBX          0  DEFCD      12                Network Game
HELP.LBX          0  DF034     232  en            In order to start, load, or join a network game, press this button. When starting a new network game or loading a saved network game, the host will then select "START" or "LOAD" to the right, all other players should  select "JOIN".
HELP.LBX          0  DF548      10                Modem Game
HELP.LBX          0  DF5AF     223  en            In order to start, load, or join a game via modem, press this button. The  player intending to initiate the call should select "START" or "LOAD" as appropriate. If you intend to wait for the host to call you, select "JOIN".
HELP.LBX          0  DFAC3      15  ?             Null Modem Game
HELP.LBX          0  DFB2A     175  en            In order to start, load, or join a game via null modem cable, press this  button. The host will select "START" or "LOAD" as appropriate, while the client should select "JOIN".
HELP.LBX          0  E003E      13  ?             Hot-Seat Game
HELP.LBX          0  E00A5     151  en            To play a game on one computer with more than one human player, select this button. Each player will be asked to choose a race, color, and player name.
HELP.LBX          0  E05B9      24  ?             Cancel Multi-Player Game
HELP.LBX          0  E0620      54  en            To return to the main menu screen, choose this option.
HELP.LBX          0  E0B34      27  ?             Start New Multi-Player Game
HELP.LBX          0  E0B9B     227  en            To start a new multi-player game, select this option. The HOST should be  the only one to select this option. He/she will have direct control over  galaxy generation parameters. All non-host players, should select  "JOIN GAME".
HELP.LBX          0  E10AF      22  ?             Load Multi-Player Game
HELP.LBX          0  E1116     381  en            To load a previously-saved multi-player game, select this option. You may continue network games as hot-seat, or vice-versa. Modem and null-modem games may also be played as either hot-seat or network games. The HOST should be  the only one to select this option. He/she will have direct control over  galaxy generation parameters. All non-host players, should select  "JOIN GAME".
HELP.LBX          0  E162A      22  ?             Join Multi-Player Game
HELP.LBX          0  E1691     284  en            To join a multi-player game, select this option. You may only join games which are currently open. If you are joining a network game, a list of open games will follow. Make sure you know which game to join before selecting this option. Only non-host players should select this option.
HELP.LBX          0  E1BA5      32  ?             Change Communications Parameters
HELP.LBX          0  E1C0C      99  en            Here is where you may change modem and null-modem parameters to fit your  computer's configuration.
HELP.LBX          0  E2120      20                Scrapping Freighters
HELP.LBX          0  E2187     149  en            Scrapping freighters will save you some maintenance costs each turn. You  will not receive any BC's, as there is not much scrap value in a freighter.
HELP.LBX          0  E269C      21                Scrapping Freighters2
HELP.LBX          0  E2702     221  en            The number in the left-most box is the minimum number of freighers you can scrap. In the right-most box is the maximum number of freighters you  may scrap. The center box shows the numbers of freighters you plan to scrap.
HELP.LBX          0  E2C17      21                Scrapping Freighters3
HELP.LBX          0  E2C7D     110  en            The left arrow button moves the bar to the left and decreases the number of freighters you wish to scrap by 1.
HELP.LBX          0  E3192      21                Scrapping Freighters4
HELP.LBX          0  E31F8     112  en            The right arrow button moves the bar to the right and increases the number of freighters you wish to scrap by 1.
HELP.LBX          0  E370D      21                Scrapping Freighters5
HELP.LBX          0  E3773      98  en            If you press the CANCEL button, you will abort this operation and no  freighters will be scrapped.
HELP.LBX          0  E3C88      21                Scrapping Freighters6
HELP.LBX          0  E3CEE      91  en            Pressing the ACCEPT button scraps the number of freighters you specified in the center box.
HELP.LBX          0  E4202      19                Communications Port
HELP.LBX          0  E4269     408  en            To play a modem or null-modem game, MOO2 needs to know which communications port to use for data transmission. This is usually the same port as your serial  card. Consult the documentation that came with your computer for more  information. \x0A\x0A When you select this field, another window will appear  showing you all of the available options. Select one from COM1 - COM7 and press the left mouse button.
HELP.LBX          0  E477D       9                Baud Rate
HELP.LBX          0  E47E4     244  en            To change the speed at which data is transmitted in modem and null-modem  games, select this box. Another window will appear showing you all of the available options. Select one by pressing the left mouse button when your choice is highlighted.
HELP.LBX          0  E4CF8      12                Phone Number
HELP.LBX          0  E4D5F      72  en            Click on this box to change the phone number of your opponents computer.
HELP.LBX          0  E5273      12                Clear String
HELP.LBX          0  E52DA     184  en            This is the modem string to clear the buffer. Click on the box to change the default string. Consult the documentation that came with your modem to insure  that the default is correct.
HELP.LBX          0  E57EE      21                Initialization String
HELP.LBX          0  E5855     188  en            This is the modem string to initialize the modem. Click on the box to change the default string. Consult the documentation that came with your modem to insure  that the default is correct.
HELP.LBX          0  E5D69      14  ?             Hang-Up String
HELP.LBX          0  E5DD0     197  en            This is the string to hang-up the modem when you are done. Click on the box to change the default string. Consult the documentation that came with your modem to insure  that the default is correct.
HELP.LBX          0  E62E4      17  ?             Tone / Pulse Dial
HELP.LBX          0  E634B     299  en            Most phone systems today use TONE dialing. However, if you live in an older  neighborhood, your modem may not be able to use TONE dialing. Click in this  box and the value will switch between TONE and PULSE. Consult the documentation that came with your modem to insure  that the default is correct.
HELP.LBX          0  E685F      20  ?             Cancel Setup Changes
HELP.LBX          0  E68C6     100  en            Pressing this button will cancel all changes you have made and return you to the main set-up screen.
HELP.LBX          0  E6DDA      20  ?             Accept Setup Changes
HELP.LBX          0  E6E41     215  en            Pressing this button will accept all changes you have made and return you to the main set-up screen. These changes will be saved to a setup file so that  once you have made changes, you will not have to do so again.
HELP.LBX          0  E7355       9                Input Box
HELP.LBX          0  E73BC     354  en            This box allows you to enter text. If you press the BACKSPACE key before pressing any other keys, all text in the box will be erased. You may also erase text by hitting CTRL-BACKSPACE at any time. When you are done, you may either press ENTER, click the RETURN button, or click inside the text area  where you are typing. To cancel, press the ESCAPE key.
HELP.LBX          0  E78D0      13                Select Banner
HELP.LBX          0  E7937     155  en            Click on the banner of the color you wish to play in the upcoming game. In multi-player games, empty boxes denote colors already selected by other players.
HELP.LBX          0  E7E4B      17                Diplomacy Request
HELP.LBX          0  E7EB2     140  en            When another player wishes to engage in diplomacy with your race, you will see this screen. You have three options, ACCEPT, IGNORE, or WAIT.
HELP.LBX          0  E83C6      24  ?             Accept Diplomacy Request
HELP.LBX          0  E842D     164  en            If you ACCEPT another player's diplomacy request, you will be taken  immediately to the diplomacy screen. Upon return, you will be sent back to the main map screen.
HELP.LBX          0  E8941      24  ?             Ignore Diplomacy Request
HELP.LBX          0  E89A8     347  en            If you IGNORE another player's diplomacy request, the requesting race will be notified and you will not be bothered with diplomacy requests from that  player. When you go to the RACES screen, you will see which races you are currently "ignoring". You will continue to ignore diplomacy requests until YOU initiate diplomacy some time in the future.
HELP.LBX          0  E8EBC      25  en            Wait on Diplomacy Request
HELP.LBX          0  E8F23     385  en            If you select WAIT, then the requesting player will be informed that you are temporarily unable to honor the request, but that you intend to meet later in the same turn. The requesting player will be informed that you intend to meet, but not immediately. He may cancel the request at any time. When you decide to meet, then go to the RACES screen and select an AUDIENCE with that race.
HELP.LBX          0  E9437      18                Shield Replacement
HELP.LBX          0  E949E     108  en            This screen allows you to change the shield type. You may remove the shield entirely by selecting NO SHIELD.
HELP.LBX          0  E99B2      23  ?             Exit Shield Replacement
HELP.LBX          0  E9A19      96  en            Clicking outside the box exits back to the main design screen without  changing the shield type.
HELP.LBX          0  E9F2D      25  ?             Cancel Shield Replacement
HELP.LBX          0  E9F94      65  en            Click the CANCEL button to exit without changing the shield type.
HELP.LBX          0  EA4A8      20                Computer Replacement
HELP.LBX          0  EA50F     114  en            This screen allows you to change the computer type. You may remove the computer entirely by selecting NO COMPUTER.
HELP.LBX          0  EAA23      25  ?             Exit Computer Replacement
HELP.LBX          0  EAA8A      98  en            Clicking outside the box exits back to the main design screen without  changing the computer type.
HELP.LBX          0  EAF9E      27  ?             Cancel Computer Replacement
HELP.LBX          0  EB005      67  en            Click the CANCEL button to exit without changing the computer type.
HELP.LBX          0  EB519      28  ?             Special System Cancel Button
HELP.LBX          0  EB580     162  en            Clicking the CANCEL button will return you to the main design screen. Regardless  of whether you were adding or replacing a system, all changes will be cancelled.
HELP.LBX          0  EBA94      27  ?             Exit Weapon Replacement Box
HELP.LBX          0  EBAFB     162  en            Clicking outside the weapon will return you to the main design screen. Regardless of whether you were adding or replacing a weapon, all changes will be cancelled.
HELP.LBX          0  EC00F      28  ?             Exit Systems Replacement Box
HELP.LBX          0  EC076     162  en            Clicking outside the weapon will return you to the main design screen. Regardless of whether you were adding or replacing a system, all changes will be cancelled.
HELP.LBX          0  EC58A      11                "No Weapon"
HELP.LBX          0  EC5F1      63  en            By selecting this item, you will clear the current weapon slot.
HELP.LBX          0  ECB05      19  es            "No Special System"
HELP.LBX          0  ECB6C      71  en            By selecting this item, you will clear the current special system slot.
HELP.LBX          0  ED080      11                "No Shield"
HELP.LBX          0  ED0E7      81  en            By selecting this item, you will be removing all shields from the current design.
HELP.LBX          0  ED5FB      13                "No Computer"
HELP.LBX          0  ED662      83  en            By selecting this item, you will be removing all computers from the current design.
HELP.LBX          0  EDB76      17                Diplomacy Options
HELP.LBX          0  EDBDD      58  en            Select the appropriate action given the current situation.
HELP.LBX          0  EE0F1      13                Self Destruct
HELP.LBX          0  EE158     112  en            This allows you to cause an explosion in your ship's drive, destroying the ship and damaging everything near it.
HELP.LBX          0  EE66C      15                Missile Warning
HELP.LBX          0  EE6D3     124  en            Toggles on/off the missile warning panel that stops a ship's movement right before a missile or fighter impacts on the ship.
HELP.LBX          0  EEBE7      15                Fast Animations
HELP.LBX          0  EEC4E      92  en            Turning Fast Animations on will speed up combat resolution at the expense of  some graphics.
HELP.LBX          0  EF162      16  ?             Show Legal Moves
HELP.LBX          0  EF1C9      81  en            Toggles on/off the tinting of all the squares to which the current ship can move.
HELP.LBX          0  EF6DD      16  ?             Show Shield Arcs
HELP.LBX          0  EF744      81  en            Toggles on/off the display of lines showing the shield arcs for the current ship.
HELP.LBX          0  EFC58      12                Display Grid
HELP.LBX          0  EFCBF      83  en            Toggles on/off the display of the square grid used to regulate movement and comabt.
HELP.LBX          0  F01D3      19  ?             Hot Seat Game Setup
HELP.LBX          0  F023A     581  en            This screen allows you to add human players to a hot seat game. While playing the game in hot-seat mode, each player takes turns playing against one another, and, perhaps, one or more computer-controlled opponenets. All players take turns using one computer which will moderate the results. After each player takes a "turn", a special menu will come up allowing you to  choose who goes next. The order of play is unimportant. \x0A\x0A Notice that to the right you will see colored squares. These denote the number of players currently added. When you are done, press  "BEGIN GAME".
HELP.LBX          0  F074E      16  ?             Add Human Player
HELP.LBX          0  F07B5     148  en            Press this button to add another human player. You will be taken through the race setup process, ie, selecting a race, race name, banner color, etc.
HELP.LBX          0  F0CC9      10                Begin Game
HELP.LBX          0  F0D30     100  en            Press this button to start the game. Empty slots will be filled with  computer-controlled opponents.
HELP.LBX          0  F1244      21  ?             Cancel Hot Seat Setup
HELP.LBX          0  F12AB      71  en            Press this button to cancel hot seat setup and return to the main menu.
HELP.LBX          0  F17BF      30  en            PLAY MASTER OF ORION II ONLINE
HELP.LBX          0  F1826     378  en            Combatting computerized Klackons is fine and dandy, but fighting  head-to-head with other humans on the Total Entertainment Network is the ultimate test of cosmic conquest. To play on TEN, you need to install  the TEN software. Go to the TEN folder in your Master of Orion directory  (default installation: c:\program files\microprose\orion2\TEN) and run the  SETUP.EXE program.
HELP.LBX          0  F1D3B       5                TEN 2
HELP.LBX          0  F1DA1     201  en            This will guide you through the TEN installation process.  After  installation, use the installed shortcut or double-click on the TEN.EXE  icon to launch TEN! \x0A\x0A ENJOY MASTER OF ORION II ON TEN!!
