MAINTEXT.LBX      0  00004      10                No Special
MAINTEXT.LBX      1  00004     198  en            A weakness in the fabric of hyperspace greatly accelerates travel between the system and another nearby system, adding +2 to the hyperspace speed of ships, but the ships must first have warp drives.
MAINTEXT.LBX      2  00004     122  en            Valuable remnants of ship wreckage are found orbiting one of the planets, and has already been quickly converted to 50 BC.
MAINTEXT.LBX      3  00004      69  en            A pirate's stash is found on one of the planets and contained 100 BC.
MAINTEXT.LBX      4  00004     148  en            One of the planets in the system contains extensive gold deposits and will generate +5 BC per turn once a colony has been established on the planet.
MAINTEXT.LBX      5  00004     148  en            One of the planets in the system contains extensive gem deposits and will generate +10 BC per turn once a colony has been established on the planet.
MAINTEXT.LBX      6  00004     280  en            Humanoid life has already begun on the world. When you land on the planet, you integrate them into your colony. Once integrated they may only work the farms, and will not leave the planet to colonize elsewhere. Furthermore, the natives do not gain the racial bonuses of your race.
MAINTEXT.LBX      7  00004     160  en            A colony once broke off from your race and formed a separate colony. The colony is small (3 population) and will want to integrate into your society once again.
MAINTEXT.LBX      8  00004     227  en            A industrialized race has colonized one of the planets in the system. Their civilization is pre-warp and cannot leave the star system. The colony is large (5 population) and they have a small fleet and will defend their system.
MAINTEXT.LBX      9  00004     105  en            A small space monster resides the star system and will attack any ships that attempt to enter the system.
MAINTEXT.LBX     10  00004     281  en            An extremely advanced civilization once inhabited this world and has inexplicably disappeared, leaving relics of wonder that adds +2 points to the research generated by each scientist on a planet. The first player to discover the system gets one or two free technology advancements
MAINTEXT.LBX     11  00004     119  en             The Guardian defends the ruins of the ancient Orion homeworld. To plunder Orion's riches you must defeat the Guardian.
MAINTEXT.LBX     12  00004      83  en            Trade Goods converts the production of a colony into BCs for the imperial treasury.
MAINTEXT.LBX     13  00004      68  en            Housing converts the production of a colony into population growth.
MSGENG.LBX        0  0046A      62  en            Titan Construction Tech is required to build TITAN class ships
MSGENG.LBX        0  00891      70  en            Doom Star Construction Tech is required to build DOOM STAR class ships
MSGENG.LBX        0  00CB8      87  en            You need to build a Star Base or a Star Fortress before you can build LARGE class ships
MSGENG.LBX        0  010DF      86  en            You need to build a Star Base or a Star Fortress before you can build HUGE class ships
MSGENG.LBX        0  01506      87  en            You need to build a Star Base or a Star Fortress before you can build TITAN class ships
MSGENG.LBX        0  0192D      91  en            You need to build a Star Base or a Star Fortress before you can build DOOM STAR class ships
MSGENG.LBX        0  01D54      61  en            Your current design is too big to fit into a SMALL class ship
MSGENG.LBX        0  0217B      62  en            Your current design is too big to fit into a MEDIUM class ship
MSGENG.LBX        0  025A2      61  en            Your current design is too big to fit into a LARGE class ship
MSGENG.LBX        0  029C9      60  en            Your current design is too big to fit into a HUGE class ship
