MSGENG.LBX        0  03A65      66  en            Since %s cannot build %s size ships, you may not change hull sizes
MSGENG.LBX        0  03E4D      15  ?             Blue-White Star
MSGENG.LBX        0  03E8C     216  en            The blue-white stars are the hottest of all the stars, emitting extreme amounts of solar radiation. The blue-white star is likely to have planets that will be mineral rich, but totally unsuitable for supporting life.
MSGENG.LBX        0  04274      10                White Star
MSGENG.LBX        0  042B3     140  en            White stars have a fair chance of having planets. If present, these planets  will be high in mineral resources, but can barely support life.
MSGENG.LBX        0  0469B      11                Yellow Star
MSGENG.LBX        0  046DA     180  en            Yellow stars are the same spectral class as our sun. The yellow star will quite frequently have planets with moderate mineral resources and a good  environment for supporting life.
MSGENG.LBX        0  04AC2      11                Orange Star
MSGENG.LBX        0  04B01     124  en            Orange stars will frequently have planets with the best chance of being habitable, but tend to be poor in mineral resources.
MSGENG.LBX        0  04EE9       8                Red Star
MSGENG.LBX        0  04F28     178  en            Red stars are the dimmest, coolest stars. The have a poor chance of having planets. If planets do exist, they will have minimal environments and extremely poor mineral resources.
MSGENG.LBX        0  05310      10                Brown Star
MSGENG.LBX        0  0534F     271  en            Brown stars are really cool! They're so cool that astronomers throughout the galaxy have been unable to put their majestic beauty into words. Perhaps after another millenium of study, our vocabulary will have been increased  sufficiently to describe these bundles of joy!
MSGENG.LBX        0  05737      11                Black Holes
MSGENG.LBX        0  05776     184  en            Black holes are ancient stars that have collapsed into a minor fraction of  their original size. So powerful are the effects of a black hole, that no  ship may pass within two parsecs.
MSGENG.LBX        0  05B5E       8                Cheating
MSGENG.LBX        0  05B9D     144  en            The High Council has found evidence that %s, the highest %s, has CHEATED!!!  Deal with this in a manner that befits the custom for your culture.
MSGENG.LBX        0  05F85      22  ?             Score Cheating Message
MSGENG.LBX        0  05FC4     217  en            Although your score is high enough to be considered amoung the greatest to  play Master Of Orion II, the High Council has decided to strip you of all  glory and accomplishment, hoping you will not CHEAT in the future!
